WEBVTT

1
00:01:32.040 --> 00:01:34.600
(HUM OF CONVERSATIONS)

2
00:01:42.080 --> 00:01:44.680
– [THUD]
– (VOICES SUBSIDE)

3
00:01:46.120 --> 00:01:48.640
[DEEP RUMBLING]

4
00:01:51.640 --> 00:01:54.760
[HELICOPTERS PASS]

5
00:02:01.760 --> 00:02:04.120
[♪ FRENETIC]

6
00:02:31.880 --> 00:02:34.480
[♪ CRESCENDO]

7
00:02:42.360 --> 00:02:43.640
YES!

8
00:02:44.720 --> 00:02:46.840
[♪ SUBSIDES]

9
00:02:51.440 --> 00:02:53.680
[RUMBLING, CREAKING]

10
00:03:22.120 --> 00:03:24.120
Ismene, listen.

11
00:03:24.240 --> 00:03:27.640
The same blood flows in both our veins,
doesn't it, my sister?

12
00:03:27.760 --> 00:03:29.480
The blood of Oedipus.

13
00:03:29.600 --> 00:03:32.720
And suffering, which was his destiny,
is our punishment, too,

14
00:03:32.840 --> 00:03:35.240
the sentence passed on all his children.

15
00:03:35.360 --> 00:03:39.920
Physical pain, contempt, insults,
every kind of dishonour –

16
00:03:40.040 --> 00:03:43.000
we've seen them all
and endured them all, the two of us.

17
00:03:44.000 --> 00:03:45.040
But there's more to come.

18
00:03:45.160 --> 00:03:49.200
Now, today, have you heard it,
this new proclamation?

19
00:03:49.320 --> 00:03:51.680
Have you heard how those nearest to us

20
00:03:51.800 --> 00:03:55.160
are to be treated with the contempt
we reserve for traitors?

21
00:03:55.280 --> 00:03:56.880
No-one has told me anything, Antigone.

22
00:03:57.000 --> 00:04:00.040
I've heard nothing, neither good nor bad
about anyone we love –

23
00:04:00.160 --> 00:04:01.600
not since the battle, I mean,

24
00:04:01.720 --> 00:04:03.080
and the terrible news
that both our brothers were dead.

25
00:04:03.200 --> 00:04:04.680
I thought you hadn't.

26
00:04:04.800 --> 00:04:07.320
That's why I asked you to meet me here,
where I could tell you everything

27
00:04:07.440 --> 00:04:11.920
– without any risk of being overheard.
– What is it, then? More terrible news?

28
00:04:12.040 --> 00:04:14.080
Something black and frightening,
I can see that.

29
00:04:14.200 --> 00:04:16.880
We have two brothers,
both of them dead.

30
00:04:17.000 --> 00:04:19.080
And Creon has decreed

31
00:04:19.200 --> 00:04:22.800
that a decent burial shall be given to one
and not to the other.

32
00:04:23.680 --> 00:04:27.960
Eteocles, apparently, has already been
buried, with full military honours

33
00:04:28.080 --> 00:04:31.680
and all the formalities due to the dead
meticulously observed

34
00:04:31.800 --> 00:04:35.720
so that his rest in the underworld
among the heroes is assured.

35
00:04:36.600 --> 00:04:42.520
But Polynices, who died in agony
just as certainly as his brother did,

36
00:04:42.640 --> 00:04:44.680
is not to be buried at all.

37
00:04:45.320 --> 00:04:47.760
The decree makes that quite plain.

38
00:04:47.880 --> 00:04:51.800
He is to be left lying where he fell,
with no tears,

39
00:04:51.920 --> 00:04:54.600
no ceremonies of mourning,

40
00:04:54.720 --> 00:05:00.040
to stink in the open till the kites
and vultures catch the scent

41
00:05:00.160 --> 00:05:03.280
and tear him to pieces
and pick him to the bone.

42
00:05:04.920 --> 00:05:10.200
Left unburied, there is no rest for him
in the underworld, no more than here.

43
00:05:10.320 --> 00:05:12.640
What a great king our Creon is,
eh, sister?

44
00:05:13.280 --> 00:05:16.200
It's against us, you realise,
and against me in particular

45
00:05:16.320 --> 00:05:18.000
he has published this decree.

46
00:05:18.120 --> 00:05:22.120
He isn't bluffing.
He means to act, to make it stick.

47
00:05:22.240 --> 00:05:28.280
The punishment for anyone who disobeys
the order is public stoning to death.

48
00:05:29.920 --> 00:05:33.000
So that's the news, and you know it now.

49
00:05:33.760 --> 00:05:37.800
The time has come for you, too,
to stand up and be counted with me,

50
00:05:37.920 --> 00:05:41.320
and to show whether you are worthy
of the honour of being Oedipus' daughter.

51
00:05:41.440 --> 00:05:43.840
– What can I do?
– [CLATTER]

52
00:05:49.520 --> 00:05:51.320
[DOOR SLAMS]

53
00:05:51.440 --> 00:05:54.640
[FOOTSTEPS WALK AWAY]

54
00:05:54.760 --> 00:05:56.480
Just say you will help me.
Commit yourself.

55
00:05:56.600 --> 00:05:59.720
– To do what? Something dangerous?
– Just give me a hand to lift the body.

56
00:05:59.840 --> 00:06:02.160
It's too heavy for me to move on my own.

57
00:06:02.280 --> 00:06:04.440
To bury him, you mean?
In spite of the decree?

58
00:06:04.560 --> 00:06:07.160
He's my brother,
and like it or not, he's yours, too.

59
00:06:07.280 --> 00:06:10.880
You must be mad!
Creon has publicly forbidden it.

60
00:06:11.000 --> 00:06:13.200
He can't forbid me to love my brother.

61
00:06:13.320 --> 00:06:15.480
He has neither the right
nor the power to do that.

62
00:06:15.600 --> 00:06:18.560
Have you forgotten
what happened to our father?

63
00:06:18.680 --> 00:06:23.600
Contempt and loathing from everyone,
even from himself, that was his reward.

64
00:06:24.200 --> 00:06:27.360
And his mother-wife,
as ill-matched with him

65
00:06:27.480 --> 00:06:31.280
as those two words are with each other,
she knotted a rope and hanged herself.

66
00:06:32.040 --> 00:06:35.600
And now our two brothers, dead on one day,

67
00:06:35.720 --> 00:06:39.720
each one cutting down the other,
blood for blood and death for death.

68
00:06:39.840 --> 00:06:44.520
We are the last ones left, sister,
and what a death is promised for us,

69
00:06:44.640 --> 00:06:47.000
more terrible than any if we break the law

70
00:06:47.120 --> 00:06:49.760
by defying the king,
and the power of the State.

71
00:06:49.880 --> 00:06:52.160
Think for a moment, Antigone, please!

72
00:06:52.280 --> 00:06:54.960
We are women, that's all –

73
00:06:55.080 --> 00:06:58.760
physically weaker,
and barred from any political influence.

74
00:06:59.400 --> 00:07:02.160
Men are in power,
and we have to obey them –

75
00:07:02.280 --> 00:07:04.600
this time
and maybe in worse situations than this.

76
00:07:05.880 --> 00:07:10.800
May God forgive me, and the spirits
of the dead, I have no choice.

77
00:07:11.680 --> 00:07:14.440
State power commands,
and I must do as I am told.

78
00:07:14.560 --> 00:07:19.320
When you are powerless, wild gestures and
heroic refusals are reserved for madmen!

79
00:07:19.440 --> 00:07:22.480
Don't say any more. I won't ask again.

80
00:07:22.600 --> 00:07:25.640
In fact, if you were to offer help now,
I would refuse it.

81
00:07:25.760 --> 00:07:28.840
Do as you please!
I intend to bury my brother.

82
00:07:28.960 --> 00:07:32.920
And if I die in the attempt, I shall die
in the knowledge that I have acted justly.

83
00:07:33.560 --> 00:07:35.040
Our lives are short.

84
00:07:35.160 --> 00:07:39.200
We have too little time to waste it
on men and the laws they make.

85
00:07:39.320 --> 00:07:41.320
The approval of the dead is everlasting,

86
00:07:41.440 --> 00:07:44.080
and I shall bask in it,
as I lie among them.

87
00:07:44.200 --> 00:07:47.480
Do as you please. Live, by all means.

88
00:07:47.600 --> 00:07:49.880
The laws you break
are not of man's making.

89
00:07:50.000 --> 00:07:54.840
I reverence them, but how can I defy
the unlimited power of the State?

90
00:07:54.960 --> 00:07:57.320
What weapons of mine
are strong enough for that?

91
00:07:57.440 --> 00:08:00.120
Fine. That's a good excuse.

92
00:08:00.240 --> 00:08:02.400
I'll go and shovel the earth
on my brother's body.

93
00:08:02.520 --> 00:08:04.880
I'm frightened, Antigone.
I'm frightened for you.

94
00:08:05.000 --> 00:08:07.760
Don't be frightened for me.
Fear for yourself.

95
00:08:07.880 --> 00:08:10.480
For God's sake, keep it quiet.
Don't tell anyone.

96
00:08:10.600 --> 00:08:12.560
– I'll keep our meeting secret.
– Don't you dare!

97
00:08:12.680 --> 00:08:15.520
You must tell everybody,
shout it in the streets.

98
00:08:15.640 --> 00:08:17.880
If you keep it secret,
I shall begin to hate you.

99
00:08:18.000 --> 00:08:21.000
This obsession will destroy you.
You're certain to fail!

100
00:08:21.120 --> 00:08:24.240
I shall fail when I have failed.
Not before.

101
00:08:24.360 --> 00:08:26.080
But you know it's hopeless.

102
00:08:26.200 --> 00:08:28.920
Why begin when you know
you can't possibly succeed?

103
00:08:29.040 --> 00:08:34.680
Be quiet, before I begin to despise you
for talking so feebly!

104
00:08:34.800 --> 00:08:37.920
Our brother will despise you, too,
and justly.

105
00:08:38.400 --> 00:08:40.080
You can go now.

106
00:08:40.200 --> 00:08:41.440
Go!

107
00:08:41.560 --> 00:08:43.680
If I'm mad, you can leave me here
to my madness

108
00:08:43.800 --> 00:08:45.960
which will doubtless
destroy me soon enough.

109
00:08:46.080 --> 00:08:48.120
Death is the worst thing that can happen,

110
00:08:48.240 --> 00:08:50.520
and some deaths are more honourable
than others.

111
00:08:50.640 --> 00:08:53.640
You've made up your mind.
Antigone, it is madness.

112
00:08:54.560 --> 00:08:56.720
Remember, I love you, whatever happens.

113
00:08:58.280 --> 00:09:00.520
[FAINT, DISTANT DRUMBEAT]

114
00:09:02.440 --> 00:09:09.400
The life-giving sun has never shone
more brightly on the seven gates of Thebes

115
00:09:09.520 --> 00:09:12.760
than he shines this morning.

116
00:09:13.800 --> 00:09:18.200
After months of blood,
our city under siege,

117
00:09:18.320 --> 00:09:22.040
last night,
our civil war reached its climax.

118
00:09:34.560 --> 00:09:39.880
Before the final night
of killing and burning,

119
00:09:40.000 --> 00:09:42.760
at the seventh gate, two brothers met.

120
00:09:44.040 --> 00:09:48.760
Eteocles, our champion,

121
00:09:48.880 --> 00:09:54.400
and Polynices, whose best hope of fame
was to conquer his native land.

122
00:09:55.640 --> 00:10:01.880
The two sons of Oedipus,
our most unfortunate king,

123
00:10:02.000 --> 00:10:05.120
shared their blood in death as in birth.

124
00:10:06.320 --> 00:10:08.440
Each brother struck together.

125
00:10:09.640 --> 00:10:13.600
Each brother laid the other dead
on the earth.

126
00:10:13.720 --> 00:10:15.200
Polynices...

127
00:10:16.720 --> 00:10:20.920
Polynices has failed in his quest.

128
00:10:24.640 --> 00:10:29.800
With their leader gone, at first light,

129
00:10:29.920 --> 00:10:34.160
his army made their panic-stricken flight!

130
00:10:34.280 --> 00:10:36.400
[BOTH LAUGH]

131
00:10:36.520 --> 00:10:39.960
And all their bright weapons were gone.

132
00:10:42.640 --> 00:10:44.320
And we have peace.

133
00:10:44.440 --> 00:10:48.280
There will be victory celebrations today
and singing in the streets.

134
00:10:48.400 --> 00:10:51.480
Time to dance all night,
to shake the foundations,

135
00:10:51.600 --> 00:10:54.000
till the faint light
of dawn flushes the windows.

136
00:10:54.120 --> 00:11:00.120
Now, with both brothers gone,
Creon is king.

137
00:11:07.680 --> 00:11:12.280
He made the most of his fortune,
and the gods' choice.

138
00:11:13.040 --> 00:11:17.440
As the people rejoice,
the new king enters to take his throne,

139
00:11:17.560 --> 00:11:20.160
the responsibility his alone.

140
00:11:29.160 --> 00:11:35.400
Our country, like a ship at sea,
has survived the hurricane.

141
00:11:37.840 --> 00:11:43.400
The gods who sent it
have navigated us into calmer waters now.

142
00:11:45.920 --> 00:11:49.440
I've chosen to summon this assembly
because I know I can trust you.

143
00:11:51.920 --> 00:11:55.000
You were loyal and reliable
when King Oedipus,

144
00:11:55.120 --> 00:11:59.320
in his exceptional wisdom,
restored the fortunes of this city.

145
00:11:59.440 --> 00:12:02.720
And when tragedy struck him
and his rule was ended,

146
00:12:02.840 --> 00:12:06.880
your loyalty to the blood royal
was never questioned,

147
00:12:07.000 --> 00:12:10.320
and you supported his sons,
till they, too, were brought down.

148
00:12:13.160 --> 00:12:18.240
By that same bloodright,
as next of kin, I claim the throne

149
00:12:18.360 --> 00:12:21.320
and all its power,
both city and kingdom.

150
00:12:23.080 --> 00:12:27.320
I claim it and hold it
from today, as mine by right.

151
00:12:33.280 --> 00:12:37.880
There is no certain measure
of a man's quality,

152
00:12:38.000 --> 00:12:42.160
the depth of his intellect
or the maturity of his judgement,

153
00:12:42.280 --> 00:12:45.120
until he is put to the supreme test

154
00:12:45.240 --> 00:12:48.360
by the exercise of lawful power
in the State.

155
00:12:48.480 --> 00:12:51.360
– My own opinion is well known.
– [CHUCKLE]

156
00:12:51.480 --> 00:12:54.720
The ruler who fears the consequences
of his actions,

157
00:12:54.840 --> 00:12:59.640
or who is afraid to act openly,
or take the good advice of his officers

158
00:12:59.760 --> 00:13:01.600
is beneath contempt.

159
00:13:01.720 --> 00:13:04.600
Equally contemptible

160
00:13:04.720 --> 00:13:07.160
is the man who puts the interests
of his friends

161
00:13:07.280 --> 00:13:10.080
or his relations, before his country.

162
00:13:11.320 --> 00:13:14.240
There is nothing good can be said of him.

163
00:13:16.280 --> 00:13:22.600
Let me make it plain before the gods,
whose eyes are in every council chamber,

164
00:13:22.720 --> 00:13:26.520
when I see any threat to this nation,
from whatever direction,

165
00:13:26.640 --> 00:13:28.400
I shall make it public.

166
00:13:30.080 --> 00:13:34.160
No one who is an enemy of the State
shall ever be any friend of mine.

167
00:13:35.560 --> 00:13:40.400
The State is everything to us,
the ship we all sail in.

168
00:13:40.520 --> 00:13:42.720
If she sinks, we all drown.

169
00:13:45.960 --> 00:13:47.040
That's my policy.

170
00:13:48.880 --> 00:13:54.040
And in pursuance of that policy,
I have issued an official State decree

171
00:13:54.160 --> 00:13:56.320
concerning the sons of Oedipus.

172
00:13:58.240 --> 00:14:02.080
Eteocles,
who died fighting for his country,

173
00:14:02.200 --> 00:14:05.440
and with exceptional bravery,

174
00:14:05.560 --> 00:14:08.320
we have buried him with all the honours
and funeral ceremonies

175
00:14:08.440 --> 00:14:10.920
customary for a man who died a hero.

176
00:14:11.040 --> 00:14:12.720
STAFF: Hear, hear.

177
00:14:13.680 --> 00:14:19.680
His brother, the exile Polynices,

178
00:14:19.800 --> 00:14:24.520
who returned here at the head of
a foreign army, to destroy his homeland,

179
00:14:24.640 --> 00:14:30.080
burn down the city and reduce
the people to a condition of slavery,

180
00:14:30.200 --> 00:14:32.080
or kill them in the streets...

181
00:14:34.000 --> 00:14:37.160
I have ordered
that he is to have no grave at all.

182
00:14:37.280 --> 00:14:38.880
[MAN LAUGHS]

183
00:14:40.440 --> 00:14:43.160
No one is to bury him or mourn for him.

184
00:14:43.280 --> 00:14:45.840
His body is to be left in the open,
uncovered,

185
00:14:45.960 --> 00:14:53.200
a stinking feast for the scavengers,
dogs and crows, a sight to inspire terror.

186
00:14:55.720 --> 00:14:59.240
I intend to make it quite plain
that never, under my administration,

187
00:14:59.360 --> 00:15:01.800
will people who commit crimes
against the State

188
00:15:01.920 --> 00:15:04.320
reap any benefit from their actions.

189
00:15:06.920 --> 00:15:10.840
But people who serve the State,

190
00:15:10.960 --> 00:15:14.160
alive or dead,
that makes no difference,

191
00:15:14.280 --> 00:15:17.120
I shall honour them for their patriotism.

192
00:15:17.960 --> 00:15:22.680
You are king now, and you have delivered
your sentence and your verdict

193
00:15:22.800 --> 00:15:24.920
upon the man who defended the city

194
00:15:25.040 --> 00:15:27.560
and the man who attacked it,
unambiguously.

195
00:15:27.680 --> 00:15:30.720
The full power of the law
is in your hands.

196
00:15:30.840 --> 00:15:32.920
It binds the dead, as well as the living.

197
00:15:33.040 --> 00:15:34.880
We are all at your disposal.

198
00:15:35.000 --> 00:15:37.160
Make sure then
that my orders are carried out.

199
00:15:37.280 --> 00:15:40.400
Younger men than us
should implement your policies.

200
00:15:40.520 --> 00:15:41.840
I don't mean that.

201
00:15:41.960 --> 00:15:44.840
– Polynices' body is already under guard.
– What else must we do?

202
00:15:44.960 --> 00:15:47.080
What other responsibility
do you lay upon us?

203
00:15:47.200 --> 00:15:51.400
Not to intrigue with dissidents
or subversive elements.

204
00:15:51.520 --> 00:15:53.040
We are not mad, sir.

205
00:15:53.160 --> 00:15:55.800
We know the law,
and the penalty for breaking it.

206
00:15:55.920 --> 00:15:59.960
Which will be death,
and be in no doubt I shall enforce it.

207
00:16:00.080 --> 00:16:04.760
Because there are always men
who can be bought, who will risk anything,

208
00:16:04.880 --> 00:16:08.080
even death, if the bribe is large enough.

209
00:16:12.360 --> 00:16:14.600
[SUBDUED VOICES]

210
00:16:19.600 --> 00:16:23.040
[CONVERSATIONS INAUDIBLE]

211
00:17:05.360 --> 00:17:07.800
[BREATHLESS GASPS APPROACHING]

212
00:17:07.920 --> 00:17:10.280
M... My Lord Creon.

213
00:17:12.640 --> 00:17:13.760
Sir!

214
00:17:17.560 --> 00:17:20.800
If I can hardly speak for lack of breath,

215
00:17:20.920 --> 00:17:22.680
it's not cos I ran.

216
00:17:22.800 --> 00:17:27.080
I kept on stopping, as a matter of fact.
'Listen, don't hurry,' I said to meself.

217
00:17:27.200 --> 00:17:29.680
'The chances are, poor sod,
you'll cop it when you get there.'

218
00:17:29.800 --> 00:17:31.240
[CREON CHUCKLES]

219
00:17:31.360 --> 00:17:33.360
But then I said to myself, you see,

220
00:17:33.480 --> 00:17:36.280
'If Creon hears this from somebody else,
you're really in trouble.'

221
00:17:36.400 --> 00:17:39.800
So, in the end, I reckoned
it would be safer to face it out.

222
00:17:39.920 --> 00:17:43.000
Talk sense, man. Why are you frightened?

223
00:17:43.120 --> 00:17:47.440
Well, first of all sir, for myself,
my own point of view...

224
00:17:49.160 --> 00:17:51.640
I never done it,
and I didn't see who else done it neither,

225
00:17:51.760 --> 00:17:53.040
so I shouldn't be punished for it,
should I?

226
00:17:53.160 --> 00:17:56.960
You take great care to disassociate
yourself from what you're saying.

227
00:17:57.080 --> 00:17:58.120
It must be bad news.

228
00:17:58.240 --> 00:18:01.960
It is bad news, sir, and I'm so scared
I don't know how to put it for the best.

229
00:18:02.080 --> 00:18:04.680
[SIGHS] The plainest way,
and then we can have done with you.

230
00:18:05.800 --> 00:18:07.440
The body's buried.

231
00:18:07.560 --> 00:18:11.840
A handful of dust, that's all,
dry dust, b-but properly sprinkled,

232
00:18:11.960 --> 00:18:14.640
you know, religiously,
and then gone, whoever it was.

233
00:18:14.760 --> 00:18:18.920
Do you know what you're saying?
Who has dared to disobey my orders?

234
00:18:20.000 --> 00:18:22.680
No way of knowing, sir. We've no idea.

235
00:18:22.800 --> 00:18:25.400
Th-There had been no digging,
no spade marks or nothing.

236
00:18:25.520 --> 00:18:26.840
The ground's rock hard.

237
00:18:26.960 --> 00:18:30.120
It was as though the body had disappeared.

238
00:18:30.240 --> 00:18:33.080
Not buried in a proper grave,
I don't mean,

239
00:18:33.200 --> 00:18:35.560
but lightly covered with a layer of earth.

240
00:18:35.680 --> 00:18:39.160
Almost as though some passing stranger
with a religious turn of mind,

241
00:18:39.280 --> 00:18:42.000
knowing that being left unburied
means everlasting anguish

242
00:18:42.120 --> 00:18:44.200
and wandering without rest,

243
00:18:44.320 --> 00:18:46.120
h-had scattered a few handfuls.

244
00:18:47.280 --> 00:18:49.360
A real row started then, I can tell you.

245
00:18:49.480 --> 00:18:52.000
We-we shouted at each other,
it could have been a fight,

246
00:18:52.120 --> 00:18:53.600
there was no one there to stop us.

247
00:18:53.720 --> 00:18:56.920
Any one of us could have done it,
we all suspected each other,

248
00:18:57.040 --> 00:18:58.880
but we all denied it.

249
00:19:00.680 --> 00:19:03.680
Called all the gods as witnesses
that we hadn't done it.

250
00:19:03.800 --> 00:19:05.680
Then one of the fellas had his say.

251
00:19:05.800 --> 00:19:07.840
He said,
'One of us lot must tell the king.

252
00:19:07.960 --> 00:19:11.320
'Because we can't just hide it,
can we?' That's what he said.

253
00:19:11.440 --> 00:19:13.240
And we knew he was right.

254
00:19:13.360 --> 00:19:17.600
S-so we decided we'd have to draw lots
and, just my luck, I drew the short straw.

255
00:19:17.720 --> 00:19:19.200
So here I am.

256
00:19:19.320 --> 00:19:22.320
And I don't like telling it one little bit
more than you like hearing it.

257
00:19:22.440 --> 00:19:24.720
The bloke who brings bad news
never gets a medal.

258
00:19:24.840 --> 00:19:26.440
(AUDIENCE LAUGHS)

259
00:19:26.560 --> 00:19:31.480
My Lord Creon, this policy of yours
has worried me from the start.

260
00:19:31.600 --> 00:19:36.400
My political instinct tells me that this
may be some sort of warning

261
00:19:36.520 --> 00:19:39.440
or sign,
and perhaps from the gods.

262
00:19:39.560 --> 00:19:42.240
How dare you?!
Shut your mouths, all of you!

263
00:19:43.360 --> 00:19:45.240
Before I lose my temper.

264
00:19:47.600 --> 00:19:53.080
Is it likely, remotely likely,
that the gods will think twice

265
00:19:53.200 --> 00:19:55.800
over that pile of stinking meat?

266
00:19:57.080 --> 00:19:59.640
By God, it's blasphemy even to suggest

267
00:19:59.760 --> 00:20:02.120
they would care a damn
whether he was buried or not!

268
00:20:03.440 --> 00:20:05.880
Let alone grant him an honourable funeral,

269
00:20:06.000 --> 00:20:09.680
as though he were one of their
principal supporters. [CHUCKLES]

270
00:20:09.800 --> 00:20:12.480
The man who came
to burn down their temples,

271
00:20:12.600 --> 00:20:15.480
plunder their treasuries,
pull down their statues

272
00:20:15.600 --> 00:20:18.960
and bring destruction and contempt
for their land and its laws?

273
00:20:21.440 --> 00:20:23.480
Do the gods love criminals these days?

274
00:20:25.400 --> 00:20:27.240
Oh, no! They do not,
but, gentlemen,

275
00:20:27.360 --> 00:20:31.920
there are men in this city and I have
noted them, a subversive faction,

276
00:20:32.040 --> 00:20:35.680
enemies of the State, a cell of
oppositionists, call them what you will,

277
00:20:35.800 --> 00:20:38.360
who reject the law and my leadership.

278
00:20:39.520 --> 00:20:42.480
They meet in secret
and nod and whisper their seditious talk,

279
00:20:42.600 --> 00:20:44.920
and they are behind this,
any fool can see that.

280
00:20:46.200 --> 00:20:48.320
Their bribery has suborned my soldiers

281
00:20:48.440 --> 00:20:51.520
and paid for this demonstration
against my authority.

282
00:20:51.640 --> 00:20:53.920
Money, gentlemen, money!

283
00:20:55.160 --> 00:20:58.920
The virus that infects mankind
with every sickness we have a name for,

284
00:20:59.040 --> 00:21:01.040
no greater scourge than that!

285
00:21:02.080 --> 00:21:04.440
Money it is that corrupts people
into doing things

286
00:21:04.560 --> 00:21:06.960
they would be ashamed to think of
before the fee was mentioned,

287
00:21:07.080 --> 00:21:11.240
and in the end leads them
into the execution chamber.

288
00:21:12.560 --> 00:21:17.400
Well, whoever they are,
these men who have sold themselves,

289
00:21:17.520 --> 00:21:20.280
they'll find the price considerably higher
than they thought it was.

290
00:21:20.400 --> 00:21:21.720
You, get this into your head.

291
00:21:23.800 --> 00:21:28.120
By Zeus, my God, whose power I revere,

292
00:21:28.240 --> 00:21:30.680
I swear to you, soldier,
either you will find the man

293
00:21:30.800 --> 00:21:33.960
who buried Polynices' body
and bring him here –

294
00:21:34.080 --> 00:21:37.200
the actual man who sprinkled the earth,
no other will do –

295
00:21:37.320 --> 00:21:40.880
standing here in front of me
or you, soldier, will die for it.

296
00:21:42.760 --> 00:21:45.640
And death, I promise you,
will be the least of your punishments.

297
00:21:45.760 --> 00:21:47.760
– The choice is yours.
– Am I allowed to speak, sir?

298
00:21:47.880 --> 00:21:52.240
No. Why should you speak?
Every word you say is painful to me.

299
00:21:52.360 --> 00:21:55.400
Maybe, but I didn't bury the body.
Not guilty to that, sir.

300
00:21:56.360 --> 00:21:59.120
But maybe guilty
of looking the other way for cash?

301
00:21:59.240 --> 00:22:00.880
I think it's a shame, sir,

302
00:22:01.000 --> 00:22:03.520
that an intelligent man
and as well educated as you are

303
00:22:03.640 --> 00:22:06.040
should miss the point so completely.

304
00:22:10.320 --> 00:22:12.520
I'm not interested in your opinions.

305
00:22:14.080 --> 00:22:16.680
If you fail to find this enemy
of the State and bring him here to me,

306
00:22:16.800 --> 00:22:20.360
you'll find that money, from whatever
source, will certainly not save your life!

307
00:22:27.640 --> 00:22:30.040
Let's hope they find him, whoever he is.

308
00:22:30.680 --> 00:22:33.240
But one thing I'm sure of,
they won't find me.

309
00:22:34.400 --> 00:22:36.240
I never thought I'd get out of here alive.

310
00:22:36.360 --> 00:22:40.600
And when I do get out,
nothing will bring me back again.

311
00:22:49.160 --> 00:22:50.720
[INAUDIBLE]

312
00:23:11.200 --> 00:23:16.280
Is there anything more wonderful on Earth
than the miracle of man?

313
00:23:23.280 --> 00:23:28.520
He has mastered the mysteries of language.

314
00:23:28.640 --> 00:23:32.560
And thought,
which moves faster than the wind,

315
00:23:32.680 --> 00:23:35.880
he has tamed and made rational.

316
00:23:38.240 --> 00:23:42.800
Political wisdom, too,
all the knowledge of people and States,

317
00:23:42.920 --> 00:23:47.480
all the practical arts of government
he has studied and refined,

318
00:23:47.600 --> 00:23:51.040
and ordered all things in his mind.

319
00:23:51.800 --> 00:23:54.120
There is no problem he cannot resolve

320
00:23:54.240 --> 00:23:57.320
by the exercise of his brains
or his breath,

321
00:23:57.440 --> 00:24:01.680
and the only disease he cannot salve
or cure...

322
00:24:03.160 --> 00:24:04.880
..is death.

323
00:24:05.680 --> 00:24:12.080
In action, he is subtle beyond
imagination, limitless in his skill,

324
00:24:12.200 --> 00:24:16.560
and these gifts are both enemies
and friends, as he applies them,

325
00:24:16.680 --> 00:24:21.280
with equal determination to good
and to evil ends.

326
00:24:23.960 --> 00:24:26.240
[TENSE PERCUSSION, SNARE DRUMROLL]

327
00:24:38.440 --> 00:24:42.760
But this is Antigone! I recognise her
as clearly as I can see you.

328
00:24:42.880 --> 00:24:45.960
– Do you have to manhandle her this way?
– We saw it!

329
00:24:46.080 --> 00:24:50.000
Actually burying the body,
caught red-handed.

330
00:24:50.120 --> 00:24:52.440
– Where's the king?
– CREON: What's all the noise?

331
00:24:52.560 --> 00:24:56.200
Just coming now –
when he's most needed.

332
00:25:11.440 --> 00:25:13.840
– What has happened?
– This girl's your criminal.

333
00:25:14.480 --> 00:25:18.160
We caught her doing it,
actually setting the grave to rights.

334
00:25:18.280 --> 00:25:21.640
I brought her here, and there was
no panic this time, I can tell you.

335
00:25:21.760 --> 00:25:25.400
No recriminations or drawing lots!
This job was all mine.

336
00:25:25.520 --> 00:25:28.320
I caught her,
and I claim the credit for it.

337
00:25:28.440 --> 00:25:31.560
And now, she's all yours.
Take her, and accuse her.

338
00:25:31.680 --> 00:25:33.680
Stone her to death, if you like.

339
00:25:33.800 --> 00:25:36.680
By rights, I'm free to go,
and well shot of all of it.

340
00:25:36.800 --> 00:25:38.000
Where did you arrest her?

341
00:25:38.120 --> 00:25:41.040
– She was burying him.
– Did you see her doing it?

342
00:25:43.440 --> 00:25:46.000
As soon as I got back,
remembering all those threats,

343
00:25:46.120 --> 00:25:48.440
or promises you made me,

344
00:25:48.560 --> 00:25:51.240
we brushed all the earth off
the naked body,

345
00:25:51.360 --> 00:25:54.360
which was all wet
and beginning to decay by now,

346
00:25:54.480 --> 00:25:57.000
and we sat up on the ridge,
well to the windward of the stink.

347
00:25:57.120 --> 00:26:00.440
For hours we sat there, till about midday.

348
00:26:00.560 --> 00:26:03.600
The sun was smack overhead, blazing down,

349
00:26:03.720 --> 00:26:07.640
and the heat was something terrible,
I can tell you.

350
00:26:07.760 --> 00:26:10.720
And then, it was as though
a whirlwind blew up,

351
00:26:10.840 --> 00:26:14.920
and it raised up a dust storm,
which swept across the plain,

352
00:26:15.040 --> 00:26:17.480
tore all the leaves off the trees,
blotted out the whole sky

353
00:26:17.600 --> 00:26:19.560
and completely blinded us.

354
00:26:19.680 --> 00:26:24.520
It seemed like some terrible
manifestation of the gods,

355
00:26:24.640 --> 00:26:27.800
and you had to shut your eyes
to endure it at all.

356
00:26:28.360 --> 00:26:31.480
And then, suddenly, it stopped.

357
00:26:31.600 --> 00:26:34.280
And when the air cleared,
we opened our eyes

358
00:26:34.400 --> 00:26:38.960
and saw this girl standing there,
beside the grave, and sort of wailing,

359
00:26:39.080 --> 00:26:42.160
as though she were in pain,
or maybe, anger.

360
00:26:42.280 --> 00:26:46.160
Just like a bird who comes back
to the nest to find the eggs smashed,

361
00:26:46.280 --> 00:26:49.160
or the fledgelings gone –
that's what it sounded like.

362
00:26:49.280 --> 00:26:53.880
She was standing there,
looking at the naked body, and screaming.

363
00:26:55.000 --> 00:26:59.440
And cursing the monsters
who had done such a thing.

364
00:26:59.560 --> 00:27:01.840
Us, of course.

365
00:27:03.320 --> 00:27:05.040
And then she crouched down,

366
00:27:05.160 --> 00:27:08.040
and she picked up a few handfuls
of the dry dust

367
00:27:08.160 --> 00:27:09.880
and she scattered it on him.

368
00:27:10.000 --> 00:27:12.800
She carried an urn,
a small ceremonial bronze thing,

369
00:27:12.920 --> 00:27:16.440
and she poured from it three times
on the dead body.

370
00:27:16.560 --> 00:27:20.400
Soon as we saw that, we came charging
down and arrested her on the spot.

371
00:27:20.520 --> 00:27:22.520
She wasn't frightened or anything.

372
00:27:22.640 --> 00:27:24.680
She stood her ground.

373
00:27:24.800 --> 00:27:27.760
So then we formally charged her
with the crime,

374
00:27:27.880 --> 00:27:30.160
this and the one before.

375
00:27:30.280 --> 00:27:32.840
She admitted she'd done them both.

376
00:27:32.960 --> 00:27:34.880
CREON: And you?

377
00:27:36.800 --> 00:27:39.000
You with your head down.

378
00:27:40.040 --> 00:27:42.440
What do you say to this accusation?

379
00:27:44.480 --> 00:27:49.800
– Do you admit it? Are you guilty, or not?
– Yes, I'm guilty.

380
00:27:49.920 --> 00:27:52.240
– I don't pretend otherwise.
– You, soldier, get out.

381
00:27:52.360 --> 00:27:55.360
You're cleared of all charges against you
and free to go back to your unit.

382
00:27:56.640 --> 00:27:58.680
CREON: Now, tell me...

383
00:28:00.480 --> 00:28:02.480
A simple yes or no.

384
00:28:02.600 --> 00:28:04.720
Did you hear of my order
forbidding the burial?

385
00:28:04.840 --> 00:28:08.600
– Of course I heard it. How could I not?
– And yet you dared to disobey the law?

386
00:28:08.720 --> 00:28:13.120
Yes, I did.
Because it's your law, not the law of God.

387
00:28:13.240 --> 00:28:16.840
Natural justice,
which is of all times and places,

388
00:28:16.960 --> 00:28:23.840
numinous, not material, a quality of Zeus,
not of kings, recognises no such law.

389
00:28:23.960 --> 00:28:27.200
You are merely a man, mortal, like me,

390
00:28:27.320 --> 00:28:30.400
and laws that you enact
cannot overturn ancient moralities

391
00:28:30.520 --> 00:28:32.960
or common human decency.

392
00:28:33.080 --> 00:28:38.240
They speak the language of eternity,
are not written down and never change.

393
00:28:38.360 --> 00:28:41.440
They are for today, yesterday
and all time.

394
00:28:42.200 --> 00:28:45.680
No one understands where they came from,
but everyone recognises their force.

395
00:28:45.800 --> 00:28:50.640
And no man's arrogance or power
could make me disobey them.

396
00:28:51.520 --> 00:28:54.720
I would rather suffer the disapproval
and punishment of men,

397
00:28:54.840 --> 00:28:57.200
than dishonour such ancient truths.

398
00:28:57.320 --> 00:29:02.320
I shall die, of course, some time,
whether you make laws or not.

399
00:29:02.440 --> 00:29:06.640
And if my death comes sooner
rather than later, I shall welcome it.

400
00:29:06.760 --> 00:29:11.840
My life has been misery – is misery now.
I shall be more than happy to leave it.

401
00:29:11.960 --> 00:29:15.000
There'll be no pain
and no despair in that.

402
00:29:15.120 --> 00:29:19.520
But to leave my mother's son
out there in the open, unburied?

403
00:29:20.440 --> 00:29:22.800
That would have been unendurable!

404
00:29:23.720 --> 00:29:25.800
I could not have borne it.

405
00:29:25.920 --> 00:29:29.520
Whereas this... I shall endure.

406
00:29:30.880 --> 00:29:32.840
By your judgement, of course, I'm a fool.

407
00:29:32.960 --> 00:29:37.200
But by mine, it is the judge,
not the accused, who's behaving foolishly.

408
00:29:37.320 --> 00:29:39.320
This is her father speaking.

409
00:29:39.440 --> 00:29:41.680
Stubborn, like him, she won't give way,

410
00:29:41.800 --> 00:29:43.840
not even with the whole power
of the State against her.

411
00:29:43.960 --> 00:29:45.800
CREON: Well, we shall see.

412
00:29:47.840 --> 00:29:50.080
Any man can be broken.

413
00:29:50.960 --> 00:29:55.200
And often the most committed
and determined break soonest.

414
00:29:55.320 --> 00:30:00.560
Even iron, you know, left lying in
the fire too long, becomes over-tempered

415
00:30:00.680 --> 00:30:03.400
and will snap as soon as
a little pressure is applied.

416
00:30:03.520 --> 00:30:05.720
You can break it in pieces.

417
00:30:08.200 --> 00:30:12.160
People without power, ordinary citizens,

418
00:30:12.280 --> 00:30:15.160
must necessarily obey
those in authority over them.

419
00:30:15.280 --> 00:30:17.440
This woman is very proud.

420
00:30:17.560 --> 00:30:20.120
That was obvious in the first place
when she broke the law,

421
00:30:20.240 --> 00:30:22.520
and is even clearer now.

422
00:30:22.640 --> 00:30:26.400
She glories in the crime she has committed
and insults me to my face,

423
00:30:26.520 --> 00:30:28.560
as well as ignoring my decree.

424
00:30:29.920 --> 00:30:32.680
If she is allowed to flout the law
in this way,

425
00:30:32.800 --> 00:30:34.920
all authority in the State will collapse.

426
00:30:35.040 --> 00:30:36.720
I will not have that!

427
00:30:38.200 --> 00:30:40.240
There will be no exchanging of roles here,

428
00:30:40.360 --> 00:30:42.640
me playing the woman
while she plays the king!

429
00:30:44.960 --> 00:30:49.240
She is my niece, my sister's child.

430
00:30:49.840 --> 00:30:53.520
But I am the law,
and that responsibility is above kinship.

431
00:30:53.640 --> 00:30:58.200
Were she even closer, the closest,
my own daughter, my duty would be plain.

432
00:31:00.520 --> 00:31:03.040
The law has its weapons
and they will strike at her

433
00:31:03.160 --> 00:31:05.040
and at her sister, too...

434
00:31:07.120 --> 00:31:09.160
..her accomplice, I've no doubt,
in this illegal act,

435
00:31:09.280 --> 00:31:11.600
to the full extent
of the punishment proscribed.

436
00:31:11.720 --> 00:31:13.640
The other one, Ismene, bring her here.

437
00:31:13.760 --> 00:31:18.200
I saw her in the corridor, talking
to herself and sobbing like a madwoman!

438
00:31:18.320 --> 00:31:20.880
Guilty conscience, you see,
can never be hidden completely.

439
00:31:21.000 --> 00:31:26.280
The human face reveals conspiracies
before they are enacted again and again.

440
00:31:28.960 --> 00:31:32.520
But there is nothing more disgusting
than the confessed criminal

441
00:31:32.640 --> 00:31:36.400
who tries to justify his actions,
as this woman has done here today.

442
00:31:36.520 --> 00:31:39.800
What more do you want?
Kill me and have done with it.

443
00:31:39.920 --> 00:31:42.080
Nothing more than your death.
That will be enough.

444
00:31:42.200 --> 00:31:44.240
Then what are you waiting for?

445
00:31:44.360 --> 00:31:46.720
Nothing you say
will be of the slightest interest to me,

446
00:31:46.840 --> 00:31:49.440
and my arguments you will not listen to.

447
00:31:49.560 --> 00:31:52.560
I've done what I said I'd do.
I've buried my brother.

448
00:31:52.680 --> 00:31:56.400
I aspire to no greater honour, and if I am
to be famous, let it be for that.

449
00:31:57.480 --> 00:32:01.160
All these, these officers of yours,
they all agree with me in their hearts.

450
00:32:01.280 --> 00:32:03.960
But there's no gag like terror,
is there, gentlemen?

451
00:32:04.080 --> 00:32:09.240
And tyrants must have their way, both in
word and action, that's their privilege!

452
00:32:09.360 --> 00:32:11.040
You are quite mistaken.

453
00:32:11.920 --> 00:32:14.440
None of the Thebans anywhere in the city
thinks as you do.

454
00:32:14.560 --> 00:32:17.240
They all do, but they keep
their mouths shut when you're here!

455
00:32:17.360 --> 00:32:20.440
Not at all! And you should be ashamed,
setting yourself up against the majority,

456
00:32:20.560 --> 00:32:24.160
– disregarding the will of the people!
– I love my brother.

457
00:32:24.280 --> 00:32:27.080
I honour him dead as I loved him living.
There's no shame in that.

458
00:32:27.200 --> 00:32:29.120
And the one he murdered?
Wasn't he your brother?

459
00:32:29.240 --> 00:32:30.800
My mother bore them both,
and I loved them both.

460
00:32:30.920 --> 00:32:34.680
– If you honour one, you insult the other.
– Neither of those dead men would say that.

461
00:32:34.800 --> 00:32:38.560
Eteocles would.
His brother was a traitor.

462
00:32:38.680 --> 00:32:40.520
Does he merit no greater respect
than that?

463
00:32:40.640 --> 00:32:42.240
He was not an animal.

464
00:32:42.360 --> 00:32:44.560
They both died together
and they were both men.

465
00:32:44.680 --> 00:32:47.240
Yes, and the one died
defending his country

466
00:32:47.360 --> 00:32:49.320
while the other traitorously attacked it!

467
00:32:49.440 --> 00:32:51.960
The dead have their rights

468
00:32:52.080 --> 00:32:55.800
and we have our duties towards them,
dictated by common decency!

469
00:32:55.920 --> 00:32:59.160
And if good and bad are to be honoured
equally, where are our values?

470
00:32:59.720 --> 00:33:01.080
Patriotism! Duty!

471
00:33:01.200 --> 00:33:03.080
Death is another country.

472
00:33:03.200 --> 00:33:06.000
Such things may not be valued there,
may even be crimes.

473
00:33:06.120 --> 00:33:08.520
An enemy is still an enemy, dead or alive.

474
00:33:08.640 --> 00:33:12.920
No, I was born with love enough to share,
no hate for anyone.

475
00:33:13.040 --> 00:33:14.720
Very well. Share your love by all means.

476
00:33:14.840 --> 00:33:16.760
Share it with the dead.
I wish them well of it.

477
00:33:18.200 --> 00:33:21.920
Women must learn to obey, as well as men.
There can be no special treatment.

478
00:33:22.040 --> 00:33:25.600
Law is law, and will remain so
while I am alive.

479
00:33:26.960 --> 00:33:28.480
No woman will get the better of me.

480
00:33:28.600 --> 00:33:31.440
MAN: Look, Ismene, weeping for her sister!

481
00:33:32.600 --> 00:33:36.320
CREON: And you! Snake!

482
00:33:37.720 --> 00:33:41.480
Slithering silently about my house,
to drink my blood in secret!

483
00:33:42.960 --> 00:33:44.840
Both of you the same!

484
00:33:44.960 --> 00:33:50.600
I looked the other way and like terrorists
you laid undercover plans to destroy me.

485
00:33:50.720 --> 00:33:54.040
Well, do you confess your complicity
in this crime

486
00:33:54.160 --> 00:33:55.800
or protest your innocence?

487
00:33:55.920 --> 00:33:58.480
Yes, I confess.
If she will allow me to say so.

488
00:33:58.600 --> 00:34:01.360
I was fully involved
and if she is guilty, so am I.

489
00:34:01.480 --> 00:34:03.640
No! That isn't justice!

490
00:34:03.760 --> 00:34:07.320
When I asked you to help me,
you refused me,

491
00:34:07.440 --> 00:34:09.560
so I told you I didn't want you,
I'd do it alone.

492
00:34:09.680 --> 00:34:12.960
But now that you're in danger, Antigone,
I'm proud to be beside you in the dock.

493
00:34:13.080 --> 00:34:14.960
The dead man knows who buried him.

494
00:34:15.080 --> 00:34:17.520
What use are people
who are all words and no action?

495
00:34:17.640 --> 00:34:21.360
Please, my sister, don't despise me!
Let me share the honour and die with you.

496
00:34:21.480 --> 00:34:25.640
You have no right to claim the honour
for doing what you were afraid to do.

497
00:34:25.760 --> 00:34:27.320
Why should you die?

498
00:34:27.440 --> 00:34:29.560
Because life without you
won't be worth living.

499
00:34:29.680 --> 00:34:31.760
Ask Creon to protect you.
He's your uncle.

500
00:34:31.880 --> 00:34:33.560
Do I deserve such contempt?

501
00:34:33.680 --> 00:34:36.120
Do you enjoy making fun of me,
sneering at my misery?

502
00:34:36.920 --> 00:34:38.520
You're right.

503
00:34:38.640 --> 00:34:42.320
It's a reflection of my own pain, if such
bitter pleasures are all I have left.

504
00:34:42.440 --> 00:34:45.840
– Let me help you then. It's not too late.
– Save your own life.

505
00:34:45.960 --> 00:34:49.240
Do that for yourself
without any criticism from me, or envy.

506
00:34:49.360 --> 00:34:51.200
For God's sake, Antigone,
will you not allow me

507
00:34:51.320 --> 00:34:52.920
even to share my death with my sister?

508
00:34:53.040 --> 00:34:54.280
No. I won't!

509
00:34:54.400 --> 00:34:57.840
You chose to live when I chose to die,
and that's the end of it.

510
00:34:57.960 --> 00:35:00.880
But I wasn't afraid to speak!
I warned you that this would happen.

511
00:35:01.000 --> 00:35:02.480
I knew how it would be!

512
00:35:02.600 --> 00:35:05.440
And most, the majority,
would agree with you.

513
00:35:05.560 --> 00:35:07.360
But some would be of my opinion.

514
00:35:07.480 --> 00:35:09.600
Then we're both in the wrong
and both condemned!

515
00:35:09.720 --> 00:35:13.040
No, you must live. I have been dead
for a long time, inwardly.

516
00:35:13.160 --> 00:35:15.560
I am well suited to pay honour
to the dead and die for it.

517
00:35:15.680 --> 00:35:17.760
These women are neurotic.

518
00:35:17.880 --> 00:35:19.600
(AUDIENCE LAUGHS)

519
00:35:21.200 --> 00:35:22.480
Lunatics, both of them!

520
00:35:22.600 --> 00:35:26.040
One of them going off her head before
our eyes, the other one born unbalanced!

521
00:35:26.160 --> 00:35:27.640
Well, are you surprised?

522
00:35:28.520 --> 00:35:32.640
Anyone would crack, the most
tough-minded person, under such treatment.

523
00:35:32.760 --> 00:35:36.920
You lost your senses when you allowed
yourself to be influenced by her lunacy.

524
00:35:37.040 --> 00:35:39.240
There's no life for me here,
not without my sister.

525
00:35:39.360 --> 00:35:42.280
Don't speak of her!
She's as good as dead.

526
00:35:42.400 --> 00:35:44.680
Will you kill the woman
your son plans to marry?

527
00:35:44.800 --> 00:35:47.560
– Well, there are other women.
– (AUDIENCE LAUGHS)

528
00:35:47.680 --> 00:35:50.840
No lack of choice for a young man,
other fields to plough.

529
00:35:50.960 --> 00:35:52.600
They're devoted to each other.

530
00:35:52.720 --> 00:35:54.920
You can't change love
as you change your clothes.

531
00:35:55.040 --> 00:35:56.720
No son of mine can marry a criminal.

532
00:35:56.840 --> 00:36:00.080
Oh, Haemon,
when you hear how your father insults you!

533
00:36:00.200 --> 00:36:03.440
Let him hear.
What does his mistress matter to me?

534
00:36:03.560 --> 00:36:06.120
– GENERAL: Lord Creon...
– INTELLIGENCE: You insult your own!

535
00:36:08.080 --> 00:36:12.800
They are formally betrothed. Will you tear
the woman from your own son's arms?

536
00:36:13.720 --> 00:36:16.520
CREON: Death parts all lovers,
sooner or later.

537
00:36:16.640 --> 00:36:20.440
GENERAL: The poor child's doomed,
her death warrant sealed and delivered.

538
00:36:20.560 --> 00:36:22.440
CREON: By you, gentlemen...

539
00:36:24.560 --> 00:36:27.600
..if you remember, as well as by me.

540
00:36:29.640 --> 00:36:32.720
You heard the order, agreed it with me,
if only by your silence, did you not,

541
00:36:32.840 --> 00:36:34.520
before the criminal was known?

542
00:36:36.160 --> 00:36:38.640
Take them away, lock them up,
keep them under close guard.

543
00:36:38.760 --> 00:36:43.200
It's time they understood they are women,
and their proper place in this society.

544
00:36:48.080 --> 00:36:50.360
There's nothing like
the immediate threat of death

545
00:36:50.480 --> 00:36:52.680
to make them look reality in the face.

546
00:37:00.680 --> 00:37:03.600
On every descendant
of the house of Oedipus,

547
00:37:03.720 --> 00:37:07.400
divine and merciless retribution falls.

548
00:37:15.760 --> 00:37:17.200
[DOOR SHUTS]

549
00:37:17.320 --> 00:37:21.920
In the unremembered past,
some unforgiving Olympian cast

550
00:37:22.040 --> 00:37:24.560
the weight of his vengeance
on the whole race,

551
00:37:24.680 --> 00:37:29.120
so that agony, destruction, disgrace

552
00:37:29.240 --> 00:37:31.240
destroys son and daughter,

553
00:37:31.360 --> 00:37:33.680
and darkens their halls
with tragedy.

554
00:37:33.800 --> 00:37:37.720
The cold hands of the dead reach out
for the living, and no one is spared.

555
00:37:37.840 --> 00:37:41.760
Another generation sheds its blood,
new light is snuffed out,

556
00:37:41.880 --> 00:37:45.440
the young root is bared
for the same bloody axe.

557
00:37:45.560 --> 00:37:50.480
The sin of Oedipus, arrogance,
brings its bleak harvest in.

558
00:37:50.600 --> 00:37:52.480
But all men hope.

559
00:37:55.280 --> 00:37:58.120
And some have ambition.

560
00:38:02.480 --> 00:38:05.440
Far-ranging birds that never tire.

561
00:38:05.560 --> 00:38:10.360
Those wings bear some men steadily onward,
but some others aimlessly swoop

562
00:38:10.480 --> 00:38:15.080
and glide down pathways to disaster
and the merciless fire.

563
00:38:15.200 --> 00:38:19.640
And no man can claim to have understood
hope or ambition,

564
00:38:19.760 --> 00:38:21.760
till the flames burn under his feet,

565
00:38:21.880 --> 00:38:26.280
and the once solid wood of his life
is reduced to its last condition –

566
00:38:26.400 --> 00:38:28.200
ashes and dust.

567
00:38:28.320 --> 00:38:33.640
A wise man said when a man commits crimes
and is proud of the action,

568
00:38:33.760 --> 00:38:36.280
a flaming sword hangs over his head.

569
00:38:36.400 --> 00:38:40.320
No future but the grave
and a funeral urn.

570
00:38:44.200 --> 00:38:47.080
Creon, here comes your youngest son.

571
00:38:47.920 --> 00:38:53.200
Is he desperate with grief that his future
bride should be so brutally denied,

572
00:38:53.320 --> 00:38:55.720
and all his hopes of happiness gone?

573
00:39:04.440 --> 00:39:06.400
My dear son.

574
00:39:15.360 --> 00:39:18.640
I don't doubt you have heard the news
of our final decision...

575
00:39:21.360 --> 00:39:23.920
..the condemnation
of the woman you intended to marry.

576
00:39:24.040 --> 00:39:28.400
You come here, I hope, not in any spirit
of anger against your father,

577
00:39:28.520 --> 00:39:35.120
but understanding that we are always
comrades, and my love for you is unshaken.

578
00:39:36.600 --> 00:39:38.680
I know I am your son, Father.

579
00:39:40.000 --> 00:39:44.960
I understand the depth of your experience
in matters of State,

580
00:39:45.080 --> 00:39:48.240
and I try to follow and benefit from it,
whenever I can.

581
00:39:49.360 --> 00:39:55.680
Any marriage would be worthless to me
that did not have your approval and love.

582
00:39:55.800 --> 00:39:59.360
– Good. Hang on to that.
– (AUDIENCE LAUGHS)

583
00:39:59.480 --> 00:40:02.520
A father's opinion should always be
influential with his son,

584
00:40:02.640 --> 00:40:07.400
and fathers with young sons,
when they pray for them,

585
00:40:07.520 --> 00:40:12.040
ask especially that they grow up
to be loyal, obedient,

586
00:40:12.160 --> 00:40:15.560
under pressure the first to strike
at their father's enemies,

587
00:40:15.680 --> 00:40:17.880
just as they are the first
to support his friends.

588
00:40:18.000 --> 00:40:19.720
Don't be taken in.

589
00:40:21.360 --> 00:40:24.800
Don't let any woman ensnare you
by exploiting her sexuality,

590
00:40:24.920 --> 00:40:29.720
or any of the attractions
that lure infatuated men into submission.

591
00:40:29.840 --> 00:40:32.640
God help the lovesick fool
who marries a dominating woman.

592
00:40:34.400 --> 00:40:38.600
Passion never lasts,
and a cold bedroom breeds cold hearts,

593
00:40:38.720 --> 00:40:40.120
anger and bitterness.

594
00:40:40.240 --> 00:40:41.960
For there's no hatred so violent

595
00:40:42.080 --> 00:40:44.480
as the hatred of two people
who were once in love.

596
00:40:44.600 --> 00:40:47.080
– Father...
– Get rid of her, my boy.

597
00:40:47.760 --> 00:40:51.760
This girl's an enemy, no good to you
or your best interests.

598
00:40:51.880 --> 00:40:53.360
Spit her out like poison.

599
00:40:53.480 --> 00:40:56.640
Let her find a husband that suits her
among the dead.

600
00:40:58.720 --> 00:41:00.320
Don't deceive yourself.

601
00:41:00.880 --> 00:41:05.120
She has been openly apprehended committing
a criminal act against the State.

602
00:41:05.240 --> 00:41:08.000
She is a confessed traitor,
and if I were to spare her life,

603
00:41:08.120 --> 00:41:11.200
I too would betray the State
and its law and everything I stand for.

604
00:41:11.320 --> 00:41:13.000
I will not do it.

605
00:41:16.280 --> 00:41:18.040
And she must die.

606
00:41:19.080 --> 00:41:21.200
Let her pray to Zeus till she drops.

607
00:41:21.320 --> 00:41:23.680
Let her assert she stands for family love

608
00:41:23.800 --> 00:41:25.880
and ancient virtues
and all the rest of it.

609
00:41:26.000 --> 00:41:29.680
If I tolerate treachery in my own house,
under my very nose,

610
00:41:29.800 --> 00:41:31.880
how can I crush subversion
anywhere in the city,

611
00:41:32.000 --> 00:41:33.520
or the State at large?

612
00:41:33.640 --> 00:41:36.840
To pervert the law,

613
00:41:36.960 --> 00:41:41.200
to twist it to serve one's own ends
or the interests of one's relations –

614
00:41:41.320 --> 00:41:44.200
that cannot be allowed,
neither in States, nor in families,

615
00:41:44.320 --> 00:41:47.560
and will not be allowed by me
in any circumstances.

616
00:41:49.360 --> 00:41:51.040
Unquestioning obedience

617
00:41:51.160 --> 00:41:55.000
to whomsoever the State appoints
to be its ruler is the law,

618
00:41:55.120 --> 00:41:58.920
as far as I'm concerned, and that applies
to small things as well as great ones,

619
00:41:59.040 --> 00:42:01.720
just or unjust, right or wrong.

620
00:42:05.320 --> 00:42:10.920
A man who is firm in his dealings with
his family will be equally firm in power.

621
00:42:11.040 --> 00:42:12.960
His wisdom will be equally remarkable,

622
00:42:13.080 --> 00:42:15.400
whether as king or, indeed, as subject.

623
00:42:16.960 --> 00:42:20.040
In times of war and national danger,

624
00:42:20.160 --> 00:42:23.880
the well-drilled regiment that asks
no questions stands firm, knows nothing,

625
00:42:24.000 --> 00:42:26.800
and needs to know nothing,
and wins!

626
00:42:29.040 --> 00:42:32.520
Thus saving the lives
of millions of honest people.

627
00:42:35.240 --> 00:42:40.080
Authority is essential in any State,
and it will be upheld in this one, by me.

628
00:42:42.040 --> 00:42:45.840
There will be no yielding to female
fantasies, not by so much as an inch.

629
00:42:47.760 --> 00:42:50.440
And if we must be deposed,

630
00:42:50.560 --> 00:42:54.880
let it be by a man's hand,
not by a conspiracy of women!

631
00:42:56.320 --> 00:43:01.000
SECRET POLICE: If I am fit to judge,
Lord Creon, you have spoken rationally,

632
00:43:01.120 --> 00:43:05.240
sensibly and with the wisdom gathered
from long experience.

633
00:43:08.160 --> 00:43:16.680
Father, the most enviable of a man's gifts
is the ability to reason clearly.

634
00:43:17.880 --> 00:43:20.720
And it's not for me to say you are wrong,

635
00:43:20.840 --> 00:43:25.560
even if I were clever enough,
or experienced enough, which I'm not.

636
00:43:27.360 --> 00:43:32.720
But it's also true to say that some men
think differently about these things.

637
00:43:33.440 --> 00:43:37.160
And as your son, my most useful function,
it seems to me,

638
00:43:37.280 --> 00:43:40.920
is to keep you in touch
with what other people are thinking.

639
00:43:41.040 --> 00:43:42.920
(AUDIENCE LAUGHS)

640
00:43:43.040 --> 00:43:46.920
The prospect of your disapproval
is a great silencer of most men's tongues,

641
00:43:47.040 --> 00:43:50.840
and some things are never said
for fear of the consequences.

642
00:43:52.640 --> 00:43:56.440
But I can sometimes hear
what people whisper behind their hands,

643
00:43:56.560 --> 00:44:03.600
and everywhere, I hear sympathy expressed
for this unfortunate girl,

644
00:44:03.720 --> 00:44:08.560
condemned, as she is,
to a horrifying death

645
00:44:08.680 --> 00:44:16.040
that no woman has ever suffered before,
and unjustly, in most people's eyes.

646
00:44:17.840 --> 00:44:19.840
In burying her brother,
who was killed in action,

647
00:44:19.960 --> 00:44:24.960
she did something most people consider
decent and honourable –

648
00:44:25.080 --> 00:44:29.400
rather than leaving him naked
on the battlefield for the dogs to tear at

649
00:44:29.520 --> 00:44:31.760
and the kites and scavengers
to pick to the bone.

650
00:44:31.880 --> 00:44:36.600
She should be given a medal for it...
those same people say,

651
00:44:36.720 --> 00:44:40.440
and her name inscribed
on the roll of honour.

652
00:44:41.920 --> 00:44:46.080
Such things are whispered in secret,
Father, and they have reached my ears.

653
00:44:47.600 --> 00:44:53.120
Sir, your reputation matters to me as much
as your good health and happiness do.

654
00:44:53.240 --> 00:44:55.640
Indeed, your good name matters more.

655
00:44:58.200 --> 00:45:01.920
So, let me beg you to have second thoughts

656
00:45:02.040 --> 00:45:05.720
and not be certain that your own opinion
is the only right one,

657
00:45:05.840 --> 00:45:07.400
and that all men share it.

658
00:45:09.240 --> 00:45:11.480
A man who thinks he has
the monopoly of wisdom,

659
00:45:11.600 --> 00:45:14.280
that only what he thinks
and what he says is of any relevance,

660
00:45:14.400 --> 00:45:17.800
reveals his own shallowness of mind
with every word he says.

661
00:45:19.200 --> 00:45:23.440
The man of judgement knows
that it is a sign of strength,

662
00:45:23.560 --> 00:45:27.320
not weakness, to value other opinions
and to learn from them,

663
00:45:27.440 --> 00:45:34.120
and when he is wrong,
to admit it openly and change his mind.

664
00:45:41.160 --> 00:45:45.280
You see it when a river floods,
the trees that bend survive.

665
00:45:45.400 --> 00:45:49.680
Those whose trunks are inflexible, are
snapped off short by the weight of water.

666
00:45:52.200 --> 00:45:55.760
I beg you, Father, think twice about this.

667
00:45:57.360 --> 00:45:59.600
Don't let your anger influence you.

668
00:46:02.520 --> 00:46:06.920
If a man of my age may lay some small
claim to common sense, let me say this.

669
00:46:08.200 --> 00:46:13.720
Absolute certainty is fine, if a man can be
certain that his wisdom is absolute.

670
00:46:15.120 --> 00:46:17.840
But such certainty and such wisdom
is rare among men,

671
00:46:17.960 --> 00:46:20.920
and that being so, the next best,
is to learn to listen

672
00:46:21.040 --> 00:46:23.320
and to take good advice when it is offered.

673
00:46:24.040 --> 00:46:31.160
There's a lot of sense, Lord Creon,
in what this young man has said.

674
00:46:31.280 --> 00:46:34.480
As indeed, there was in everything
that you said, too.

675
00:46:34.600 --> 00:46:39.520
– (AUDIENCE LAUGHS)
– The fact is, you are both in the right,

676
00:46:39.640 --> 00:46:41.680
and there's a good deal to be said
for either.

677
00:46:41.800 --> 00:46:43.360
Is there, indeed?

678
00:46:46.400 --> 00:46:48.240
Am I expected to listen

679
00:46:48.360 --> 00:46:52.120
and take lessons in political tactics
at my age, from a mere boy?

680
00:46:52.240 --> 00:46:56.480
I'm a man, Father,
and my arguments are just.

681
00:46:56.600 --> 00:46:58.480
They stand upon their merits, not my age.

682
00:46:58.600 --> 00:47:01.280
Oh, they, er...
stand upon their merits, do they?

683
00:47:01.400 --> 00:47:04.360
Well, what merit is there, please tell me,
in breaking the law?

684
00:47:04.480 --> 00:47:07.080
If she'd done something shameful
I wouldn't defend her.

685
00:47:07.200 --> 00:47:09.600
She's brought the law into contempt.
That's shameful.

686
00:47:09.720 --> 00:47:14.680
Listen to the people in the street,
Father, the ordinary Thebans!

687
00:47:14.800 --> 00:47:16.080
They say she hasn't!

688
00:47:16.200 --> 00:47:20.240
I have never based my political principles
on the opinions of people in the street!

689
00:47:20.760 --> 00:47:22.800
Now you're the one
who's speaking like a boy!

690
00:47:25.760 --> 00:47:27.640
I'm speaking like a king.

691
00:47:28.400 --> 00:47:32.920
It's my responsibility, and I will act
according to my own convictions.

692
00:47:33.040 --> 00:47:37.000
When the State becomes one man
it ceases to be a State.

693
00:47:37.120 --> 00:47:39.880
The State is the statesman who rules it.

694
00:47:40.000 --> 00:47:42.720
It reflects his judgement,
it belongs to him!

695
00:47:43.520 --> 00:47:45.840
Go and rule in the desert, then!

696
00:47:46.760 --> 00:47:49.800
There's nobody there to argue with you.
What a king you'll be there!

697
00:47:54.920 --> 00:47:58.440
This boy of mine is on the woman's side.

698
00:47:58.560 --> 00:48:02.000
I'm on your side, Father.
I'm fighting for you.

699
00:48:02.120 --> 00:48:06.000
Every word you have spoken is against me,
your own father.

700
00:48:06.120 --> 00:48:08.280
When I know you are wrong,
I have to speak.

701
00:48:08.400 --> 00:48:10.120
How am I wrong?

702
00:48:10.240 --> 00:48:13.640
By maintaining my authority and
the position of the State? Is that wrong?

703
00:48:13.760 --> 00:48:18.480
When position and authority
ride roughshod over moral feeling...

704
00:48:18.600 --> 00:48:23.560
You're weak and uxorious and contemptible,
with no will of your own.

705
00:48:23.680 --> 00:48:26.600
– You're a woman's mouthpiece!
– I'm not ashamed of what I'm saying.

706
00:48:26.720 --> 00:48:29.040
Every word you have said
pleads for her cause.

707
00:48:29.160 --> 00:48:36.240
I plead for you, and for myself and for
common humanity, respect for the dead!

708
00:48:36.360 --> 00:48:39.960
You will never marry that woman,
she won't live long enough to see that day.

709
00:48:40.080 --> 00:48:43.320
If she dies, she won't die alone.

710
00:48:45.280 --> 00:48:48.040
There'll be two deaths, not one.

711
00:48:48.160 --> 00:48:49.880
Are you threatening me?

712
00:48:50.000 --> 00:48:53.360
– How dare you threaten...?
– It's not a threat. I'm telling you.

713
00:48:53.480 --> 00:48:55.680
Your policy was misbegotten
from the beginning.

714
00:48:55.800 --> 00:49:00.080
If anything is misbegotten here, it's
my son. You'll regret this, I promise you.

715
00:49:00.200 --> 00:49:02.280
If you weren't my father,
I'd say you were demented.

716
00:49:02.400 --> 00:49:05.680
Don't father me!
You're a lap dog, a woman's plaything.

717
00:49:05.800 --> 00:49:07.920
Is anyone else allowed to speak?

718
00:49:09.560 --> 00:49:13.600
Must you have the last word in everything,
must all the rest of us be gagged?

719
00:49:13.720 --> 00:49:15.760
I must, and I will,
and you, I promise you,

720
00:49:15.880 --> 00:49:18.040
will regret what you have spoken here
today.

721
00:49:18.160 --> 00:49:23.560
I will not be sneered at
or contradicted by anyone!

722
00:49:24.560 --> 00:49:27.040
Sons can be punished, too, you know.
Bring her out.

723
00:49:27.160 --> 00:49:30.600
The bitch, let her die here and now,
in the open,

724
00:49:30.720 --> 00:49:33.400
with her bridegroom beside her
as a witness!

725
00:49:35.440 --> 00:49:37.840
You can watch the execution.

726
00:49:38.840 --> 00:49:41.240
That's one sight I shall never see!

727
00:49:43.320 --> 00:49:48.000
Nor from this moment, Father,
will you ever see me again.

728
00:49:53.800 --> 00:49:59.600
Those that wish to stay
and watch this disgusting spectacle

729
00:49:59.720 --> 00:50:02.760
in company with a madman,
are welcome to it!

730
00:50:02.880 --> 00:50:07.640
Lord Creon, an uncontrollable fury
has possessed your son

731
00:50:07.760 --> 00:50:09.800
and swept him off like a whirlwind.

732
00:50:09.920 --> 00:50:12.040
A young man's anger is a terrifying thing!

733
00:50:12.160 --> 00:50:16.360
Let him go and shout his head off
about moral this and decent that,

734
00:50:16.480 --> 00:50:17.880
till he raves himself senseless!

735
00:50:18.000 --> 00:50:20.320
The two women are sentenced.

736
00:50:21.040 --> 00:50:23.960
It will take more than bluster
to reprieve them, I promise you.

737
00:50:24.080 --> 00:50:25.320
Both of them, sir?

738
00:50:25.440 --> 00:50:27.800
You mean to put both
of the sisters to death?

739
00:50:28.440 --> 00:50:33.080
No. You're right. I can take advice.

740
00:50:35.440 --> 00:50:37.360
The one who covered the body,
not the other.

741
00:50:37.480 --> 00:50:40.400
And for the condemned one,
what manner of death?

742
00:50:43.480 --> 00:50:48.240
Take her to some lonely place,
rocky and unfrequented by anyone.

743
00:50:48.360 --> 00:50:51.440
Find a cave and wall her up in it.
Bury her alive.

744
00:50:53.320 --> 00:50:55.880
But with just enough food
so that no guilt for her death

745
00:50:56.000 --> 00:50:58.200
falls either upon us or on the State.

746
00:51:00.080 --> 00:51:02.640
She'll have plenty of time
to honour the gods of the dead there.

747
00:51:02.760 --> 00:51:06.200
Since they receive so many of her prayers,
they will release her.

748
00:51:09.360 --> 00:51:13.080
And she'll learn that worshipping the dead
is not the business of the living.

749
00:51:18.640 --> 00:51:21.840
When the god
of unbridled passion makes war,

750
00:51:21.960 --> 00:51:23.600
he always wins.

751
00:51:23.720 --> 00:51:28.480
No force on Earth can withstand
his powerful, merciless hand.

752
00:51:28.600 --> 00:51:34.080
The gods themselves run mad.
Men lose their wits, and no one is spared.

753
00:51:34.920 --> 00:51:38.000
What else could provoke this strife
between father and son,

754
00:51:38.120 --> 00:51:42.120
a family divided,
and murderous anger between kin?

755
00:51:42.240 --> 00:51:44.280
There is fire in a woman's eye.

756
00:51:45.240 --> 00:51:49.120
In such consuming heat,
a man's mind can burn.

757
00:51:52.840 --> 00:51:55.520
[♪ TENSE TONES]

758
00:52:17.000 --> 00:52:19.080
[DISTANT BELL TOLLS]

759
00:52:51.680 --> 00:52:53.880
[SINISTER RUMBLING]

760
00:53:25.920 --> 00:53:28.480
[RUMBLING, METALLIC GRATING]

761
00:53:33.040 --> 00:53:36.400
Yet how can we talk of justice
and the needs of the State

762
00:53:36.520 --> 00:53:40.040
while we sit and watch
this unendurable sight?

763
00:53:40.160 --> 00:53:45.280
In all my wanderings, gentlemen,
this place has been my home.

764
00:53:49.120 --> 00:53:53.920
I was born in this city,
and now I begin my last journey.

765
00:53:54.520 --> 00:53:57.160
I look up at the sun in its familiar sky

766
00:53:57.280 --> 00:54:00.240
and feel its warmth on my face
only to say goodbye.

767
00:54:01.080 --> 00:54:06.280
To the cold waters of darkness I come,
never to return across that silent river.

768
00:54:06.400 --> 00:54:08.560
But your action is famous.

769
00:54:09.320 --> 00:54:11.920
On every street,
mouths whisper 'Antigone'.

770
00:54:12.040 --> 00:54:16.440
You go down to the dead with the promise
of glory ringing in your head

771
00:54:16.560 --> 00:54:19.960
and nothing to devalue your beauty.

772
00:54:20.640 --> 00:54:23.160
No sword has scarred you, plague visited.

773
00:54:24.160 --> 00:54:29.120
Unmarked, untouched,
you pass from the dangerous light

774
00:54:29.240 --> 00:54:31.600
into the safety of eternal night,

775
00:54:31.720 --> 00:54:35.280
alive, alone and free.

776
00:54:35.400 --> 00:54:38.560
Do you remember the sad story
of Tantalus' daughter, Niobe?

777
00:54:38.680 --> 00:54:42.360
She was unmarried, like me,
in danger, like mine.

778
00:54:42.480 --> 00:54:44.760
She was sentenced to die
on the rock of Sipylus,

779
00:54:44.880 --> 00:54:49.680
and there was no glory for her,
only the endless shock of the elements

780
00:54:49.800 --> 00:54:52.160
and the terrible place
where she was imprisoned.

781
00:54:52.280 --> 00:54:56.280
The mountain's embrace like fingers of ivy
tying her down,

782
00:54:56.400 --> 00:55:00.400
enclosing, entombing her,
and she all alone.

783
00:55:01.160 --> 00:55:05.120
What bitter tears she shed
as she slowly turned to stone,

784
00:55:05.240 --> 00:55:08.520
and the grey rock petrified her by inches,
and she died.

785
00:55:08.640 --> 00:55:10.080
Her story is mine.

786
00:55:10.200 --> 00:55:14.480
She was a goddess.
Can her story really help you?

787
00:55:15.080 --> 00:55:19.160
Or will it soften your distress
to pretend you are a child of the gods?

788
00:55:19.280 --> 00:55:22.840
If you say it often enough,
perhaps it will become the truth.

789
00:55:22.960 --> 00:55:24.560
This is a mockery!

790
00:55:24.680 --> 00:55:32.600
By everything the city of our fathers
has ever held sacred, my dying is no joke!

791
00:55:32.720 --> 00:55:38.680
Then, forests and meadows
and our Theban river, ceaselessly flowing,

792
00:55:38.800 --> 00:55:42.360
you must be my witnesses, my only mourners

793
00:55:42.480 --> 00:55:48.440
as, victimised by an unjust law,
I go to my last home to wait,

794
00:55:48.560 --> 00:55:51.560
while the slow darkness descends,

795
00:55:51.680 --> 00:55:56.560
cold and starving on my stony bed,
halfway between the living and the dead.

796
00:55:56.680 --> 00:56:01.120
No one has ever dared to go so far before
as you have dared to go.

797
00:56:01.240 --> 00:56:05.000
You carry your father's crimes
like a millstone on your back.

798
00:56:05.920 --> 00:56:10.760
Small wonder, in such times,
if the bones bend or break.

799
00:56:10.880 --> 00:56:17.080
Nothing more painful than that,
the remembrance of my father's long agony,

800
00:56:17.200 --> 00:56:20.960
and the curse on my suffering family
from the beginning.

801
00:56:21.080 --> 00:56:27.480
So much grief from the unlucky chance
of the son finding the mother's bed,

802
00:56:27.600 --> 00:56:29.280
and worse than anything,

803
00:56:29.400 --> 00:56:32.000
the desperate offspring
of that unspeakable marriage –

804
00:56:32.120 --> 00:56:34.520
and I share that terrible destiny.

805
00:56:35.120 --> 00:56:39.920
Conceived in incest, no repentance
can soften the punishment.

806
00:56:40.040 --> 00:56:45.680
The years pass, the agonies increase
and there is no pity for our tears.

807
00:56:47.160 --> 00:56:49.760
No marriage for me, for certain.

808
00:56:49.880 --> 00:56:53.120
I shall close that book forever,
the weddings will cease.

809
00:56:53.240 --> 00:56:57.160
To pay respect to the dead
is praiseworthy, an act of love,

810
00:56:57.280 --> 00:56:58.800
and religion must have its due.

811
00:56:58.920 --> 00:57:03.080
But laws must be obeyed,
whether we approve or disapprove.

812
00:57:03.200 --> 00:57:05.320
Spare me your sympathy.

813
00:57:05.440 --> 00:57:08.840
I know the path that I must follow,

814
00:57:08.960 --> 00:57:12.160
to the sunless country of eternal sorrow,

815
00:57:12.280 --> 00:57:17.520
to the bleak waters of eternity,
the unimaginable years.

816
00:57:17.640 --> 00:57:20.560
No grief where none is felt.

817
00:57:20.680 --> 00:57:24.960
I shall go alone
and in silence to my house of stone.

818
00:57:25.080 --> 00:57:28.680
If death could be prevented
by singing arias about it,

819
00:57:28.800 --> 00:57:31.480
or other self-indulgent displays of grief,

820
00:57:31.600 --> 00:57:34.120
this performance would go on forever,
I've no doubt.

821
00:57:36.200 --> 00:57:38.160
But I've had enough of it.

822
00:57:38.280 --> 00:57:40.520
Take her away,
lock her up in her stone vault

823
00:57:40.640 --> 00:57:43.280
with half a mountain for a roof,
then brick up the door.

824
00:57:43.400 --> 00:57:44.800
Let her die there, if she chooses.

825
00:57:44.920 --> 00:57:48.400
Or if she prefers,
stay alive in her grave – why not?

826
00:57:49.760 --> 00:57:54.080
Whatever she does, there will be
no guilt on me, or on the State.

827
00:57:54.200 --> 00:57:56.640
Her death's her own,

828
00:57:56.760 --> 00:57:59.200
but there is no place for her
among the living.

829
00:57:59.320 --> 00:58:01.200
To my grave, then.

830
00:58:01.320 --> 00:58:07.920
My honeymoon bed, my prison, my crypt,
my home for the rest of time.

831
00:58:08.040 --> 00:58:10.240
I shall see so many of my relations there.

832
00:58:10.360 --> 00:58:13.280
I am the last, the unhappiest,
I think, and the youngest,

833
00:58:13.400 --> 00:58:16.840
but my father will be there
to meet me at the door.

834
00:58:16.960 --> 00:58:21.280
And mother will smile and hold me close,
as she always did.

835
00:58:21.400 --> 00:58:26.800
And my brother, he will be glad to see me,
more than all the rest.

836
00:58:26.920 --> 00:58:31.080
At each fresh grave
my hands sprinkled the earth,

837
00:58:31.200 --> 00:58:34.640
at each I poured the purifying waters
and made offerings.

838
00:58:34.760 --> 00:58:40.640
And for my beloved Polynices,
whose broken body I set to rest,

839
00:58:40.760 --> 00:58:44.880
I am rewarded with a shameful death!

840
00:58:45.840 --> 00:58:50.920
There are some, I know, more
thoughtful people, who respect my action.

841
00:58:51.040 --> 00:58:53.160
You must justify me!

842
00:58:53.680 --> 00:58:57.840
Not for a husband, you understand.
Not even for a son would I have done it.

843
00:58:57.960 --> 00:59:02.600
If the law had forbidden it, I would have
bowed my head and let them rot.

844
00:59:02.720 --> 00:59:05.240
I could have married again,
another husband,

845
00:59:05.360 --> 00:59:08.200
had more children by him,
if the first had died.

846
00:59:08.320 --> 00:59:11.680
Do you see? Do you understand me?

847
00:59:11.800 --> 00:59:14.840
But my mother and father are dead.

848
00:59:15.560 --> 00:59:18.040
There can be no more brothers,
never again.

849
00:59:18.160 --> 00:59:22.880
My love had to speak at Polynices' grave,
or nowhere.

850
00:59:23.000 --> 00:59:27.040
And for that terrible crime,
my dearest brother,

851
00:59:27.160 --> 00:59:29.640
Creon sentences me to death,

852
00:59:29.760 --> 00:59:34.240
drags me here, and will shut me away
in a cavern under a mountain,

853
00:59:34.360 --> 00:59:39.680
a living death
in silence and darkness and solitude.

854
00:59:39.800 --> 00:59:42.680
I shall die unmarried,

855
00:59:42.800 --> 00:59:46.560
all those pleasures denied me,
and motherhood denied, too.

856
00:59:46.680 --> 00:59:49.720
No children to love me, to love!

857
00:59:49.840 --> 00:59:52.440
And now, no friends.

858
00:59:52.560 --> 00:59:55.840
What moral law have I broken?

859
00:59:55.960 --> 00:59:58.320
What eternal truths have I denied?

860
00:59:58.440 --> 01:00:00.840
Yet now, not even a god can help me,

861
01:00:00.960 --> 01:00:02.760
and there's no man who will,
I'm sure of that.

862
01:00:02.880 --> 01:00:04.760
No help and no hope!

863
01:00:04.880 --> 01:00:09.200
How can there be,
when common decency has become a crime?

864
01:00:09.920 --> 01:00:12.840
If the gods in heaven
have changed their minds,

865
01:00:12.960 --> 01:00:16.520
and this is the way they order
things now, I shall soon know it,

866
01:00:16.640 --> 01:00:19.400
and I will have learned my lesson
the hard way.

867
01:00:19.520 --> 01:00:21.080
But if some others are mistaken,

868
01:00:21.200 --> 01:00:24.440
let them be punished
as I have been punished,

869
01:00:24.560 --> 01:00:27.720
and suffer the injustice I suffer!

870
01:00:27.840 --> 01:00:29.880
She hasn't changed, even now.

871
01:00:30.000 --> 01:00:32.560
The anger inside her blows up,
like a hurricane.

872
01:00:32.680 --> 01:00:35.480
The sooner she's got rid of, out of harm's
way and forgotten about the better.

873
01:00:35.600 --> 01:00:38.840
– Get a move on, or you'll regret it!
– That word is my death.

874
01:00:40.480 --> 01:00:43.560
And now it's spoken.
Don't comfort yourself with hope.

875
01:00:44.320 --> 01:00:47.600
– There's none.
– This is the land of my fathers, Thebes.

876
01:00:47.720 --> 01:00:49.480
Built by a god!

877
01:00:49.600 --> 01:00:52.320
You see, my time has run out,
there is no more left.

878
01:00:52.440 --> 01:00:56.400
I am the last of the royal blood,
a daughter of kings.

879
01:00:56.520 --> 01:01:00.160
And I die his victim, unjustly...

880
01:01:00.280 --> 01:01:05.320
[VOICE RECEEDING].. for upholding justice
and the humanity of humankind!

881
01:01:19.520 --> 01:01:22.280
Fate has its own momentum.

882
01:01:23.520 --> 01:01:26.880
When things must be, they will be.

883
01:01:27.920 --> 01:01:31.760
What use is power in the State,
or wealth, massive armies,

884
01:01:31.880 --> 01:01:33.720
an unsinkable fleet?

885
01:01:33.840 --> 01:01:37.360
The Gods make their entrances by strength
or stealth,

886
01:01:37.480 --> 01:01:40.080
and no tombs or towers can keep them out.

887
01:01:41.040 --> 01:01:43.640
Man's fate is determined,
cannot be denied.

888
01:01:44.480 --> 01:01:47.960
The child Antigone
pays for the parents' pride.

889
01:01:49.880 --> 01:01:52.440
[BIRDSONG]

890
01:01:58.400 --> 01:02:01.280
[BIRDSONG CONTINUING]

891
01:02:14.080 --> 01:02:16.120
[BIRDSONG STOPS]

892
01:02:29.680 --> 01:02:32.880
[ELECTRICITY BUZZING, FIZZING]

893
01:02:33.000 --> 01:02:34.680
Agh!

894
01:02:34.800 --> 01:02:37.840
[CRASHING WHITE NOISE]

895
01:02:55.200 --> 01:02:57.600
MAN: [DISTANT] Citizens of Thebes!

896
01:02:59.080 --> 01:03:02.280
And your new king, Creon!

897
01:03:03.840 --> 01:03:07.400
We have travelled together, my boy and I,

898
01:03:07.520 --> 01:03:10.600
sharing one pair of eyes
between the two of us –

899
01:03:10.720 --> 01:03:14.320
which is the way blind men
must make their journeys.

900
01:03:14.440 --> 01:03:19.480
Teiresias!
What news brings you so far?

901
01:03:19.600 --> 01:03:21.600
Important news that can't wait,

902
01:03:21.720 --> 01:03:24.800
and advice which, if you're wise,
you'll listen to.

903
01:03:24.920 --> 01:03:28.960
I've always listened –
and acted upon it more than once!

904
01:03:29.080 --> 01:03:35.160
And like a sensible captain who values
his pilot, you've avoided the rocks.

905
01:03:35.280 --> 01:03:38.480
I admit it. We all do.

906
01:03:38.600 --> 01:03:41.600
– We are in your debt.
– Then for God's sake, listen to me now.

907
01:03:42.440 --> 01:03:49.200
You're like a man balanced on a razor,
likely to fall – or cut himself to pieces.

908
01:03:49.840 --> 01:03:52.800
Any man would shudder
hearing such things from your lips

909
01:03:52.920 --> 01:03:54.760
which have foretold so many horrors.

910
01:03:54.880 --> 01:03:57.480
– Tell me what you mean.
– Oh, yes. I intend to.

911
01:03:57.600 --> 01:04:00.640
Everything my experience
of forecasting the future

912
01:04:00.760 --> 01:04:05.560
and understanding symbols has revealed
to me, I will make plain to you.

913
01:04:05.680 --> 01:04:08.040
I was sitting in my usual seat –

914
01:04:08.160 --> 01:04:13.720
a place where I can hear the singing
and the secret language of the birds

915
01:04:13.840 --> 01:04:17.640
and understand their meaning –
when I heard, quite unexpectedly,

916
01:04:17.760 --> 01:04:19.960
a terrible new sound,

917
01:04:20.080 --> 01:04:24.560
like shrieking, or cries of anguish.

918
01:04:25.640 --> 01:04:32.120
Hysterical twittering and whistling
like the babble of a barbaric language

919
01:04:32.240 --> 01:04:35.280
only capable of expressing hatred or pain.

920
01:04:35.400 --> 01:04:41.880
By that, and the wild beating of wings,
I knew the birds were at war.

921
01:04:43.560 --> 01:04:45.880
Such sounds could mean nothing else.

922
01:04:46.680 --> 01:04:52.320
I could well imagine their bloodstained
beaks and dripping claws,

923
01:04:52.440 --> 01:04:54.840
and that thought disturbed me deeply.

924
01:04:54.960 --> 01:05:00.720
At once, I went to my altar to see what
I could learn from the sacrifice by fire.

925
01:05:02.200 --> 01:05:04.720
But nothing would burn.

926
01:05:05.720 --> 01:05:11.600
A filthy liquid ran from the flesh
and dropped on the embers –

927
01:05:11.720 --> 01:05:14.800
and sizzled and bubbled among the ashes.

928
01:05:14.920 --> 01:05:18.760
Then the gall bladder burst...

929
01:05:20.120 --> 01:05:24.040
..spurting stinking acid across the meat.

930
01:05:24.160 --> 01:05:28.720
And all the fat melted,

931
01:05:28.840 --> 01:05:32.800
and was rendered down
till the bone was left bare.

932
01:05:34.360 --> 01:05:37.320
I saw all this – or my boy saw it.

933
01:05:37.440 --> 01:05:40.000
He sees for me what my eyes cannot,

934
01:05:40.120 --> 01:05:43.400
just as I see things
to which other people are blind.

935
01:05:44.400 --> 01:05:48.240
But in that filth I read nothing.

936
01:05:49.520 --> 01:05:53.400
The oracle was clogged with fat and decay.

937
01:05:53.520 --> 01:05:55.240
And then...

938
01:05:56.120 --> 01:05:58.280
..it was revealed.

939
01:05:58.400 --> 01:06:02.760
I understood that you, King Creon,

940
01:06:02.880 --> 01:06:07.440
have decreed this filth
that chokes our altars.

941
01:06:07.560 --> 01:06:11.360
The blood and flesh that decays
and stinks there

942
01:06:11.480 --> 01:06:17.960
is the blood and flesh vomited from
the gullets of dogs and carrion crows,

943
01:06:18.080 --> 01:06:20.840
the blood of Polynices.

944
01:06:21.960 --> 01:06:26.200
The flesh of that unluckiest
of sons of Oedipus,

945
01:06:26.320 --> 01:06:28.600
still unburied,

946
01:06:28.720 --> 01:06:31.760
and affronting more
than our sense of smell.

947
01:06:32.560 --> 01:06:37.680
The gods themselves are disgusted.

948
01:06:38.560 --> 01:06:43.120
They reject our prayers and sacrifices.
How could they do otherwise?

949
01:06:43.240 --> 01:06:46.800
How can the birds sing
of anything but horrors,

950
01:06:46.920 --> 01:06:51.560
blown out with this banquet
of human blood,

951
01:06:51.680 --> 01:06:56.400
clogged and stinking,
till their very beaks drip with it?

952
01:06:56.520 --> 01:06:58.600
My friend, listen to me.

953
01:06:59.360 --> 01:07:02.360
Any man can make a mistake
or commit a crime.

954
01:07:02.480 --> 01:07:05.480
The man who can recognise
what he has done,

955
01:07:05.600 --> 01:07:09.480
see that he was mistaken
or morally wrong,

956
01:07:09.600 --> 01:07:11.960
admit it and put it right,

957
01:07:12.080 --> 01:07:17.120
that man proves that it is never too late
to become wise,

958
01:07:17.240 --> 01:07:20.000
and no one will condemn him.

959
01:07:21.760 --> 01:07:28.600
But if he compounds his stupidity
with stubbornness

960
01:07:28.720 --> 01:07:34.200
and an obstinate refusal to face the facts,
he is nothing but a fool.

961
01:07:35.320 --> 01:07:38.040
Is there anyone more stupid

962
01:07:38.160 --> 01:07:42.440
than the stupid man
who cannot see his own stupidity?

963
01:07:43.440 --> 01:07:49.440
Polynices is dead.
Don't revenge yourself on his remains.

964
01:07:49.560 --> 01:07:52.320
You can kill a man once,
and once only.

965
01:07:52.440 --> 01:07:56.480
Is there any glory to be gained
by defeating a poor corpse?

966
01:07:56.600 --> 01:08:03.160
This is good advice, my friend, sincerely
offered by someone who wishes you well.

967
01:08:04.120 --> 01:08:05.520
Take it.

968
01:08:07.840 --> 01:08:10.600
So, that's your news, is it?

969
01:08:12.320 --> 01:08:17.160
I am to be the target, am I,
for everyone to shoot at?

970
01:08:20.040 --> 01:08:21.480
Well...

971
01:08:23.000 --> 01:08:24.440
I'm wise, too.

972
01:08:26.720 --> 01:08:29.760
Wise to the ways of fortune-tellers,

973
01:08:29.880 --> 01:08:32.720
and the buying and selling
you all go in for.

974
01:08:34.320 --> 01:08:37.520
And I'm to be the latest bargain,
I see, ha-ha!

975
01:08:37.640 --> 01:08:42.320
I'm to be bought and sold, like silver.
I'm to be part of the trade!

976
01:08:44.000 --> 01:08:45.600
Let me tell you this.

977
01:08:46.840 --> 01:08:50.640
There is not enough gold in the world
to buy a grave for that man.

978
01:08:52.320 --> 01:08:58.720
If golden eagles should carry him up
by joints and shreds to Zeus

979
01:08:58.840 --> 01:09:04.240
and spew him in gobbets
on the marble floors of Olympus,

980
01:09:04.360 --> 01:09:08.880
not even that blasphemy would be enough
to deflect me from my purpose.

981
01:09:10.760 --> 01:09:18.000
Because I know that no single human act,
however much it may degrade the earth,

982
01:09:18.120 --> 01:09:21.800
can stain the purity
of the ever-living gods.

983
01:09:23.720 --> 01:09:28.840
But let me tell you this, Teiresias,
a man can fall.

984
01:09:31.320 --> 01:09:33.800
He can fall like a stone,

985
01:09:33.920 --> 01:09:37.360
especially when he pretends
to give good advice

986
01:09:37.480 --> 01:09:41.320
and wraps it up
in a profound cloak of religiosity,

987
01:09:41.440 --> 01:09:46.880
when all the time, naked self-interest
and the greed for profit

988
01:09:47.000 --> 01:09:49.320
are the only motives that matter to him.

989
01:09:49.440 --> 01:09:53.160
– Are there any wise men left? Anywhere?
– Goodness, how profound(!)

990
01:09:53.280 --> 01:09:56.360
Do you have any more
thunderous platitudes to follow that one?

991
01:09:56.480 --> 01:09:59.240
Mature judgment cannot be bought!

992
01:09:59.360 --> 01:10:01.920
No treasure is as valuable,

993
01:10:02.040 --> 01:10:06.040
and good advice is worth more
than a fortune to any man.

994
01:10:06.160 --> 01:10:10.520
And bad advice is worse than worthless,
a disease which infects the wisest of men.

995
01:10:11.360 --> 01:10:14.320
I refuse to become involved
in a slanging match

996
01:10:14.440 --> 01:10:16.920
or quarrel
with the recognised prophet of Thebes!

997
01:10:17.040 --> 01:10:19.080
And yet you insult me to my face.

998
01:10:19.200 --> 01:10:22.400
You say my predictions are both false
and dishonest.

999
01:10:22.520 --> 01:10:25.440
That is because all fortune-tellers
are money grabbers and charlatans.

1000
01:10:25.560 --> 01:10:30.440
Oh, kings... kings, too,
have been known to be acquisitive.

1001
01:10:30.560 --> 01:10:32.840
Do you realise the man
you are speaking to? I am the king!

1002
01:10:32.960 --> 01:10:38.280
You are the king, yes.
My good advice helped to make you one.

1003
01:10:38.400 --> 01:10:41.960
– You've had your successes, I admit it.
– (AUDIENCE LAUGHS)

1004
01:10:42.080 --> 01:10:44.000
You've been right
on more than one occasion,

1005
01:10:44.120 --> 01:10:45.920
but honesty's another matter.

1006
01:10:46.040 --> 01:10:48.600
– I've never trusted you.
– [CRIES OUT] No!

1007
01:10:48.720 --> 01:10:53.320
Don't provoke me to tell you everything!

1008
01:10:53.440 --> 01:10:58.240
The dark waters of prophecy
are better left undisturbed.

1009
01:10:58.360 --> 01:11:02.920
Disturb them, I don't care! Say anything
at all, but say it honestly, not for cash!

1010
01:11:03.040 --> 01:11:09.760
Are you really foolish enough to believe
that money has ever been my motive?

1011
01:11:09.880 --> 01:11:12.320
Because my integrity is not for sale!

1012
01:11:12.440 --> 01:11:17.560
[SHOUTS ANGRILY] Listen, Creon!
This is the truth!

1013
01:11:17.680 --> 01:11:20.640
Before many more days,
before the sun has risen –

1014
01:11:20.760 --> 01:11:24.880
Well, shall we say a few more times? –

1015
01:11:25.000 --> 01:11:28.640
you will have made your payment,
corpse for corpse,

1016
01:11:28.760 --> 01:11:31.920
with a child of your own blood.

1017
01:11:32.560 --> 01:11:35.320
You have buried the one still living!

1018
01:11:35.440 --> 01:11:40.640
The woman who moves and breathes,
you have given to the grave.

1019
01:11:40.760 --> 01:11:44.920
And the dead man you have left, unwashed,

1020
01:11:45.040 --> 01:11:51.080
unwept and without the common courtesy
of a decent covering of earth.

1021
01:11:51.200 --> 01:11:54.160
So that both have been wronged,

1022
01:11:54.280 --> 01:11:59.440
and the gods of the underworld,
to whom the body justly belongs,

1023
01:11:59.560 --> 01:12:02.800
are denied it and are insulted.

1024
01:12:02.920 --> 01:12:06.240
Such matters are not for you to judge.

1025
01:12:07.440 --> 01:12:11.440
You usurp ancient rights

1026
01:12:11.560 --> 01:12:16.200
which even the gods themselves
don't dare to question,

1027
01:12:16.320 --> 01:12:20.800
powers which are not
in the prerogative of kings.

1028
01:12:20.920 --> 01:12:27.200
Even now, implacable avengers
are on their way –

1029
01:12:27.320 --> 01:12:33.520
the Furies, who rise up from Hell
and swoop down from Heaven,

1030
01:12:33.640 --> 01:12:37.520
fix their hooks
into those who commit crimes

1031
01:12:37.640 --> 01:12:40.720
and will never let go!

1032
01:12:40.840 --> 01:12:45.280
The suffering you inflicted upon others
will be inflicted upon you.

1033
01:12:45.400 --> 01:12:48.360
You will suffer, as they did.

1034
01:12:49.800 --> 01:12:51.760
Have I been bribed, do you think?

1035
01:12:51.880 --> 01:12:55.240
Am I speaking for money now? Huh?

1036
01:12:55.360 --> 01:12:57.240
Before very long...

1037
01:12:59.480 --> 01:13:01.880
[CALMLY] Yes, it will be soon,

1038
01:13:02.000 --> 01:13:05.760
there will be shrieking and bitter tears

1039
01:13:05.880 --> 01:13:09.760
and hysterical crying in this house.

1040
01:13:10.680 --> 01:13:13.120
Men, as well as women.

1041
01:13:13.240 --> 01:13:18.920
Other cities too, other States, will turn
upon you for the crime you have committed.

1042
01:13:19.040 --> 01:13:23.080
Dogs and vultures
will swarm in their streets,

1043
01:13:23.200 --> 01:13:27.000
dropping fragments of the unburied man
at corners,

1044
01:13:27.120 --> 01:13:29.920
on doorsteps, in the public squares.

1045
01:13:30.040 --> 01:13:33.920
They will smell the pollution,
and turn to you,

1046
01:13:34.040 --> 01:13:35.760
its author!

1047
01:13:37.560 --> 01:13:39.480
[WHIMPERING]

1048
01:13:44.080 --> 01:13:46.120
That's all I have to say.

1049
01:13:48.280 --> 01:13:52.840
You made me angry, Creon,
with your crude accusations.

1050
01:13:52.960 --> 01:13:59.400
So I made you my target, and like a good
marksman, all my shots have hit the bull.

1051
01:14:01.760 --> 01:14:03.760
Take me home now, boy.

1052
01:14:06.440 --> 01:14:11.200
Leave him alone
to entertain some younger ears than mine

1053
01:14:11.320 --> 01:14:13.320
with his ridiculous outbursts.

1054
01:14:13.440 --> 01:14:18.720
Either that, or let him learn
maturer judgement,

1055
01:14:18.840 --> 01:14:24.360
and how a wise man controls his tongue.

1056
01:14:41.360 --> 01:14:43.120
He's gone, my lord.

1057
01:14:44.720 --> 01:14:47.360
Promising nothing but disasters to come.

1058
01:14:51.080 --> 01:14:53.840
I grew grey in this city.

1059
01:14:55.440 --> 01:14:58.160
I was dark-haired here
and now I'm white, ha!

1060
01:15:00.080 --> 01:15:05.480
And in all that time, I have never known
any of his prophecies to be proved wrong.

1061
01:15:05.600 --> 01:15:07.520
Neither have I, man.

1062
01:15:08.600 --> 01:15:10.680
I know that much as well as you.

1063
01:15:14.720 --> 01:15:19.840
My mind's torn apart, like a tug of war,
one way, then the other.

1064
01:15:19.960 --> 01:15:22.720
How can I give way now?

1065
01:15:22.840 --> 01:15:25.240
How can I stand here like a fool

1066
01:15:25.360 --> 01:15:28.200
and wait stubbornly
for whatever disaster may be coming?

1067
01:15:28.320 --> 01:15:31.480
Lord Creon, it's time to take good advice.

1068
01:15:31.600 --> 01:15:33.360
Give it then. Don't be afraid.
I'll listen.

1069
01:15:33.480 --> 01:15:35.960
Release the woman
from her underground prison.

1070
01:15:36.080 --> 01:15:37.800
And give honourable burial
to the dead man.

1071
01:15:37.920 --> 01:15:40.120
Oh, so that's your advice?

1072
01:15:40.240 --> 01:15:41.960
(AUDIENCE LAUGHS)

1073
01:15:42.080 --> 01:15:46.520
Total collapse, complete withdrawal!
Do you all think that?

1074
01:15:46.640 --> 01:15:50.400
– We do, sir.
– And do it quickly, for heaven's sake!

1075
01:15:50.520 --> 01:15:53.000
The gods never move faster
than when punishing men

1076
01:15:53.120 --> 01:15:55.040
with the consequences
of their own actions.

1077
01:15:56.000 --> 01:15:57.480
How can I do it?

1078
01:15:58.600 --> 01:16:04.520
It's unendurable to deny every principle
and action I have stood fast by.

1079
01:16:06.120 --> 01:16:09.760
Yet I dare not stand
against the iron laws of necessity.

1080
01:16:09.880 --> 01:16:12.720
– Go on, sir.
– Do it now, and do it personally.

1081
01:16:12.840 --> 01:16:14.840
Not by proxy, with your own hands.

1082
01:16:18.040 --> 01:16:19.400
Yes.

1083
01:16:21.600 --> 01:16:24.240
I'll go myself, at once!

1084
01:16:25.000 --> 01:16:29.400
Somebody, everybody, bring spades
and sledge-hammers – I'm coming with you!

1085
01:16:31.480 --> 01:16:36.160
If I've changed my mind, I'll act upon it
with exactly the same determination.

1086
01:16:36.280 --> 01:16:40.040
I sentenced her, and I'll set her free,

1087
01:16:40.160 --> 01:16:43.200
tear down the bricks with my own hands
if necessary.

1088
01:16:45.040 --> 01:16:48.040
Perhaps it's wiser
to let the old laws stand.

1089
01:16:48.160 --> 01:16:50.800
My fear tells me it is.

1090
01:16:52.240 --> 01:16:55.280
And that's a voice
every prudent man must listen to.

1091
01:17:03.320 --> 01:17:05.680
[DEEP RUMBLING]

1092
01:17:39.880 --> 01:17:48.560
Great God with many names,
Bacchus, Dionysus.

1093
01:17:51.000 --> 01:17:55.200
This is your native city, your own Thebes.

1094
01:17:55.320 --> 01:18:01.960
Now in your city disaster threatens,
fear locks up our tongues

1095
01:18:02.080 --> 01:18:09.120
and, like a plague sore on the face,
the State's disease is made public.

1096
01:18:11.840 --> 01:18:15.960
– We have done wrong.
– Now the first necessity is for healing.

1097
01:18:17.760 --> 01:18:22.200
Come to us, healer, and heal.
We have suffered too long.

1098
01:18:28.720 --> 01:18:30.800
[GASPING]

1099
01:18:33.280 --> 01:18:35.080
[RETCHING, GASPING]

1100
01:18:38.880 --> 01:18:41.240
What kind of life can there be,

1101
01:18:41.360 --> 01:18:44.720
when the things that make life pleasant
are destroyed?

1102
01:18:44.840 --> 01:18:48.680
Of course, he's rich beyond accounting,
he's a king still,

1103
01:18:48.800 --> 01:18:54.000
with all the pomp and circumstance
that rank implies.

1104
01:18:54.120 --> 01:18:59.120
But what's it worth
when all the joy of life is gone?

1105
01:18:59.240 --> 01:19:02.240
– More tragedy for this family?
– Tell us the news.

1106
01:19:02.360 --> 01:19:05.760
They're both dead,
and the living must take the blame.

1107
01:19:05.880 --> 01:19:08.360
– Who killed them?
– Who's dead? What happened? Tell us!

1108
01:19:08.480 --> 01:19:12.640
The king's son, Haemon.
The royal blood shed by the royal hand.

1109
01:19:12.760 --> 01:19:16.080
– His father's you mean? Or his own?
– His own held the sword.

1110
01:19:16.200 --> 01:19:18.520
But his father's actions drove it home.

1111
01:19:18.640 --> 01:19:21.120
The prophet warned us
and it all came true.

1112
01:19:22.000 --> 01:19:25.200
Eurydice, poor woman, Creon's wife.

1113
01:19:25.320 --> 01:19:27.720
– Does she know, do you think?
– Gentlemen.

1114
01:19:29.800 --> 01:19:31.400
Good friends.

1115
01:19:34.240 --> 01:19:36.960
My ears caught something
of what you were saying,

1116
01:19:37.080 --> 01:19:39.600
a few words, as I opened the door.

1117
01:19:41.880 --> 01:19:46.720
I was on my way to offer prayers
to Pallas Athene,

1118
01:19:46.840 --> 01:19:50.560
when I heard a few scraps
of your conversation.

1119
01:19:52.640 --> 01:19:56.320
Enough to make me fear
what all mothers fear.

1120
01:19:58.280 --> 01:20:04.120
An accident or some disaster
to those we love.

1121
01:20:05.720 --> 01:20:12.600
I almost fainted. Please!
Speak it out plainly, whatever it is.

1122
01:20:12.720 --> 01:20:14.680
I can bear it.

1123
01:20:14.800 --> 01:20:19.160
We are bred to stoicism in this family.

1124
01:20:19.280 --> 01:20:24.320
Dear queen, whom we all respect...

1125
01:20:25.840 --> 01:20:30.040
I was there, I saw it all,
and I'll tell you exactly what happened.

1126
01:20:30.160 --> 01:20:36.200
There's no point in trying to soften the
blow now, only to be proved a liar later.

1127
01:20:37.280 --> 01:20:39.320
It's best to tell the truth.

1128
01:20:42.560 --> 01:20:45.960
I went with the king, your husband,
to the edge of the battlefield,

1129
01:20:46.080 --> 01:20:48.480
where we saw the body of Polynices,

1130
01:20:48.600 --> 01:20:51.160
still lying where he fell
and in a terrible state.

1131
01:20:51.280 --> 01:20:56.160
The dogs had been at him,
so we washed him, or what was left of him,

1132
01:20:56.280 --> 01:21:00.720
with holy water,
cut fresh branches to make a pyre,

1133
01:21:00.840 --> 01:21:02.280
and burned the remains.

1134
01:21:02.400 --> 01:21:07.520
Then we shovelled a mound of his own
Theban earth over the ashes.

1135
01:21:07.640 --> 01:21:13.400
Then after we had finished, we hurried off
to the prison cell furnished with stones

1136
01:21:13.520 --> 01:21:17.280
that served as a bridal suite
for the girl married to death.

1137
01:21:17.400 --> 01:21:20.760
But before we arrived,

1138
01:21:20.880 --> 01:21:26.200
one of the soldiers with the unenviable job
of guarding that god-forsaken place,

1139
01:21:26.320 --> 01:21:30.480
came running back to tell the king
he'd heard a terrible noise,

1140
01:21:30.600 --> 01:21:33.640
like screaming,
coming from inside the mountain.

1141
01:21:33.760 --> 01:21:38.520
And as Creon got nearer,
he heard it, too – faint, but audible,

1142
01:21:38.640 --> 01:21:43.600
a weird kind of sobbing or moaning,
low and unearthly,

1143
01:21:43.720 --> 01:21:48.200
as if grief were speaking
its own naked language.

1144
01:21:48.320 --> 01:21:51.680
The king groaned aloud,
and we all heard him say,

1145
01:21:51.800 --> 01:21:55.760
'Oh, God, this is what I was afraid of.
Am I a prophet, too?'

1146
01:21:55.880 --> 01:22:01.240
And then, 'You, quickly, guards, anybody,
get inside, squeeze between the rocks.

1147
01:22:01.360 --> 01:22:03.640
'Where somebody
has already forced an entrance,

1148
01:22:03.760 --> 01:22:05.880
'get into the main chamber of the cave

1149
01:22:06.000 --> 01:22:10.400
'and tell me
if it is my son's voice I recognised.

1150
01:22:11.440 --> 01:22:14.480
'Or if the gods are playing
some brutal game with me.'

1151
01:22:14.600 --> 01:22:16.960
So, we went in.

1152
01:22:18.200 --> 01:22:23.400
And in the darkest corner, we saw her,
strung up by the neck,

1153
01:22:23.520 --> 01:22:31.320
hanging from an improvised rope of twisted
linen strips torn from her own dress.

1154
01:22:32.160 --> 01:22:36.840
Haemon was right beside her,
clawing at her body as it dangled there,

1155
01:22:36.960 --> 01:22:40.160
sobbing broken-heartedly
at his wife's death,

1156
01:22:40.280 --> 01:22:44.720
and the marriage bad luck
and his father's cruelty had made certain

1157
01:22:44.840 --> 01:22:46.440
would never take place.

1158
01:22:46.560 --> 01:22:51.080
When Creon saw them,
he staggered into the cave,

1159
01:22:51.200 --> 01:22:57.080
groaning like an animal, and sobbed aloud,
'My boy, my poor boy, what have you done?'

1160
01:22:57.200 --> 01:22:59.960
And then, 'Have you gone mad, coming here?

1161
01:23:00.080 --> 01:23:03.240
'There's nothing here for you
but death and annihilation and despair.

1162
01:23:03.360 --> 01:23:05.120
'Come away from here, my boy.

1163
01:23:05.240 --> 01:23:08.560
'Come out, for God's sake,
I'm begging you, come away!'

1164
01:23:08.680 --> 01:23:13.040
But the boy just looked at him
and his eyes were terrifying.

1165
01:23:13.160 --> 01:23:18.520
Without a word,
he spat in his father's face,

1166
01:23:18.640 --> 01:23:22.040
drew his sword
and lunged straight for your husband.

1167
01:23:22.160 --> 01:23:24.840
But Creon was quick
and skipped out of distance.

1168
01:23:24.960 --> 01:23:31.200
And the poor lad,
hysterical with grief and self-disgust,

1169
01:23:31.320 --> 01:23:34.840
held the sword at arm's length
and p...

1170
01:23:36.000 --> 01:23:40.600
..plunged it between his own ribs.

1171
01:23:45.120 --> 01:23:46.760
And then...

1172
01:23:49.200 --> 01:23:56.240
..still conscious, he lifted the girl down
into the crook of his arm

1173
01:23:56.360 --> 01:24:00.120
and cradled her there in his own blood.

1174
01:24:01.200 --> 01:24:03.840
His breathing got harder and shorter,

1175
01:24:03.960 --> 01:24:08.440
as the life flooded away
before our eyes, like a fountain,

1176
01:24:08.560 --> 01:24:14.080
soaking her body so that her white cheeks
flushed red again with the bloodstains.

1177
01:24:20.040 --> 01:24:23.920
So, now they're together,
two corpses, joined in death.

1178
01:24:24.480 --> 01:24:28.520
He got his marriage, poor lad,
but it was solemnised in the grave

1179
01:24:28.640 --> 01:24:30.760
where there are no celebrations.

1180
01:24:30.880 --> 01:24:34.200
They looked like honeymooners,

1181
01:24:34.320 --> 01:24:38.320
quietly sleeping side-by-side in one bed.

1182
01:24:39.360 --> 01:24:42.120
Evidence of the havoc
man can bring upon man

1183
01:24:42.240 --> 01:24:45.160
by his own pig-headedness and arrogance.

1184
01:24:45.280 --> 01:24:49.200
That's strange.
His wife has gone without a word.

1185
01:24:50.760 --> 01:24:53.480
She'll suffer, like any other mother,
for her son's death,

1186
01:24:53.600 --> 01:24:55.920
but in private, with her women.

1187
01:24:56.480 --> 01:24:59.760
She'd never do anything foolish
or indiscreet, I'm sure of that.

1188
01:24:59.880 --> 01:25:01.360
I don't know.

1189
01:25:01.480 --> 01:25:05.920
That sort of silence is sometimes
more threatening than screaming and tears.

1190
01:25:06.040 --> 01:25:07.520
[DEEP RUMBLING]

1191
01:25:07.640 --> 01:25:09.400
I'll go in after her.

1192
01:25:39.120 --> 01:25:41.440
There was a hatred inside me.

1193
01:25:44.280 --> 01:25:47.080
The urge to destroy
drove me like a maniac.

1194
01:25:50.440 --> 01:25:52.720
An insane plunge towards death.

1195
01:25:56.960 --> 01:25:58.560
Your death, my boy.

1196
01:26:05.080 --> 01:26:09.880
I was responsible. My actions killed him.
There is no blame for him, none.

1197
01:26:13.280 --> 01:26:15.560
Blasted in the morning of your life.

1198
01:26:18.240 --> 01:26:21.520
My hope, my joy.

1199
01:26:24.280 --> 01:26:28.800
My hand powered the knife,
my arrogance determined your fate.

1200
01:26:28.920 --> 01:26:31.960
INTELLIGENCE: You see the truth now,
but you see it too late.

1201
01:26:32.840 --> 01:26:35.600
Suffering is the only schoolteacher.

1202
01:26:38.000 --> 01:26:41.840
The gods have broken my back
and destroyed my self-respect.

1203
01:26:44.240 --> 01:26:51.240
Man is a naked, mortal creature.
Affliction is all he can expect.

1204
01:26:51.360 --> 01:26:56.160
My Lord, you have suffered enough,
but more suffering is marked to your name.

1205
01:26:56.280 --> 01:26:59.120
One agony lies here in the open,
another is waiting,

1206
01:26:59.240 --> 01:27:02.280
the same anguish redoubled,
behind the door.

1207
01:27:03.480 --> 01:27:07.760
There can be nothing worse.
My heart is broken.

1208
01:27:09.120 --> 01:27:11.880
MESSENGER: Your wife is dead,

1209
01:27:12.000 --> 01:27:13.920
the mother to this slaughtered son.

1210
01:27:14.040 --> 01:27:17.320
Her wound is fresh,
but the breath of life is gone.

1211
01:27:19.560 --> 01:27:23.160
Will you kill me, too?

1212
01:27:25.760 --> 01:27:28.360
Or bring me to my knees to suffer longer?

1213
01:27:29.840 --> 01:27:33.560
What can you say, messenger of death,
more than you've said already?

1214
01:27:33.680 --> 01:27:36.680
– There's no hiding it now!
– See for yourself!

1215
01:27:48.920 --> 01:27:54.280
This is the second time I am forced to see
what no man's eyes should ever see,

1216
01:27:54.400 --> 01:27:56.440
even once.

1217
01:27:58.120 --> 01:28:00.000
Is this how it ends?

1218
01:28:00.120 --> 01:28:03.400
Or will there be more torture,
more suffering?

1219
01:28:05.320 --> 01:28:10.360
A few moments ago,
my trembling arms embraced a dead son.

1220
01:28:10.480 --> 01:28:13.840
Now, death has snatched the mother
from my hands.

1221
01:28:13.960 --> 01:28:17.560
I found her collapsed
and as she closed her eyes, she wept

1222
01:28:17.680 --> 01:28:23.680
for the son whose life ended today,
and with her last, dying breath,

1223
01:28:23.800 --> 01:28:28.800
cursed you as his murderer,
who drove him to this death.

1224
01:28:28.920 --> 01:28:30.800
She spoke the truth.

1225
01:28:32.280 --> 01:28:34.320
All the guilt is mine.

1226
01:28:34.440 --> 01:28:36.520
I am the murderer. Make that plain!

1227
01:28:38.840 --> 01:28:43.760
Somebody, anybody, take me away.
I disgrace the decent light of day.

1228
01:28:43.880 --> 01:28:45.960
I am nothing.

1229
01:28:48.000 --> 01:28:50.360
I have become nothing.

1230
01:28:55.160 --> 01:28:58.160
Nothing can happen
to a man who is nothing.

1231
01:28:58.280 --> 01:29:00.960
ANALYST: How can we judge for the best
in times like these?

1232
01:29:02.120 --> 01:29:04.600
– Prompt action is safest.
– What more is there to lose?

1233
01:29:05.960 --> 01:29:09.200
CREON: Where are you, death?
My friend, come.

1234
01:29:09.320 --> 01:29:13.360
Wrap me in your darkness,
as a friend should. Why waste another day?

1235
01:29:13.480 --> 01:29:15.800
Tomorrow is a mystery.

1236
01:29:15.920 --> 01:29:18.640
No man can say
what time will make plain.

1237
01:29:18.760 --> 01:29:22.600
We live day by day.
The future is in greater hands than ours.

1238
01:29:22.720 --> 01:29:27.960
I am nothing. I want nothing.
My last, simplest prayers.

1239
01:29:28.080 --> 01:29:32.000
INTELLIGENCE: There's time for prayers now.
It's too late to pray!

1240
01:29:32.120 --> 01:29:36.360
What must come will come,
tomorrow or today.

1241
01:29:36.480 --> 01:29:38.200
I am nothing!

1242
01:29:41.480 --> 01:29:45.040
Take... me then.

1243
01:29:47.200 --> 01:29:50.400
The man who killed, without knowing it,
his wife and son.

1244
01:29:54.360 --> 01:29:56.240
Where shall I go?

1245
01:29:57.680 --> 01:29:59.360
Left or right?

1246
01:30:03.120 --> 01:30:05.360
All wrong turnings now.

1247
01:30:06.240 --> 01:30:09.360
Into the night,
darkness, hide me.

1248
01:30:10.160 --> 01:30:12.120
There's blood on my hands.

1249
01:30:13.880 --> 01:30:15.560
My head is split.

1250
01:30:17.200 --> 01:30:18.480
My back is broken.

1251
01:30:21.680 --> 01:30:23.440
I should be dead.

1252
01:30:27.400 --> 01:30:32.960
SECURITY: The key to human happiness
is to nurture wisdom in your heart,

1253
01:30:33.080 --> 01:30:37.800
for man to attend to man's business
and let the gods play their part.

1254
01:30:37.920 --> 01:30:44.640
Above all, to stand in awe
of the eternal, unalterable law.

1255
01:30:45.520 --> 01:30:51.960
The proud man may pretend in his arrogance
to despise everything but himself.

1256
01:30:52.080 --> 01:30:56.080
In the end,
the gods will bring him to grief.

1257
01:30:58.120 --> 01:30:59.840
Today, it happened here.

1258
01:31:02.800 --> 01:31:05.680
[MILITARY DRUMS, RUMBLING, CREAKING]

1259
01:31:38.000 --> 01:31:40.160
[DRUMS STOP]

1260
01:31:43.400 --> 01:31:46.240
(APPLAUSE, CHEERS)

1261
01:32:16.320 --> 01:32:17.960
(HUGE CHEER)
